{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants","id":872276,"title":"Making Muslim-based and Jewish-based vampire Covenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T04:25:50-07:00","id":872276,"title":"Making Muslim-based and Jewish-based vampire Covenants","content":"So, this has come up several times. A number of people want to see a muslim-based covenant for a number of reasons. And, despite no real calls for it, there should be consideration for jewish faith as well - jews aren't christian-lite, and we should not treat them as such.<br /> <br /> So, I'm going to write out an outline for the two, and people who are interested in creating these homebrew covenants can suggest adding things in. The Iblic Creed / Benu Shaitan an Dammitic creed were written with the eye to become Lancea Creeds, so don't feel constrained by that. Lets hear all ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT - names are merely placeholders, so feel free to make suggestions to change those as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-23-2016, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:30:54-07:00","id":872277,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Ibn-Shaitan</span><br /> The Fivefold Pillars </div> <br /> <i>Fiction blurb</i><br /> <br /> <b>You want to join the covenant because:</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Big Picture:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Our Practices</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames</b><br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><br /> <br /> <b>When we are in power:</b><br /> <br /> <b>When we are in trouble:<br /> <br /> Covenant Advantages / merits:</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:32:04-07:00","id":872278,"title":"","content":"This was the vague Muslim outline I had written before, and it's explanation. It needs some serious reworking, and I find it still slightly too close to the LeS for my current tastes, but for consideration.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">First of all, I want to stress the reasons for why this new Covenant is necessary.<br /> The Faith of Longinus requires Muslims (and Jews, but I\u2019m mostly concerned with Muslims here) to deny certain base Muslim beliefs. Primarily, it requires them to deny that Muhammad is the Seal of the Prophets. Seal of the Prophets has a dual meaning, both of which must be respected. Firstly, it means that his revelations abrogate all previous revelations. Secondly, it means that his revelations are the final revelations, and cannot be abrogated (except internally).<br /> The Faith of Longinus requires a Muslim to believe that the revelations of Longinus are still relevant after Muhammad\u2019s revelations, and thus have not been abrogated. This requires a Muslim to cease to believe in one of the central statements of Islam, that Muhammad is the Seal of the Prophets, and thus for a Muslim to become a Longinan, they first have to cease to be a Muslim.<br /> A Muslim covenant has to address the vampiric condition from a Muslim standpoint. It has to emerge naturally from Muslim thought. It thus cannot be based on any text or scripture from before Muhammad. Nor can it be based on any text or scripture from after Muhammad, as Muhammad was the last of Prophets, and no revelation can come after him. Thus, the Covenant has to be based in a revelation of Muhammad.<br /> Yet how to reconcile this without dramatically changing the story of Muhammad? When the Qur\u2019an was compiled, a few decades after the death of Muhammad, they had a system to ensure that no false verse was added. People had committed verses to memory, or written down passages, often on cattle shoulder-blades. A certain number of people had to corroborate a verse for it to be added. As the story goes, the Caliph himself remembered a verse, yet because it could not be corroborated, it was not added, despite his authority. What if verses were discovered that could not be corroborated at the time, but seemed to refer to the vampiric condition?<br /> A second, since discredited theory, mostly held by sceptical Western scholars refusing to believe the traditional account due to the need at the time to discredit Muslim histories, held that Islam was invented as a religion closer to Mesopotamia and the area known as al-Jazira, to address a new need for a belief system to justify a new empire, in a land where many religions mixed and debated. While I think this theory is a load of bumpkis, I do think that parts of it can be used for the history of the new covenant. Here follows a quick history of the Covenant.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">On the most part, the Kindred of the Middle East did not convert to Islam. They were ancient beings, some predating even Christianity, many holding to pagan faiths. Up until the 9<sup>th</sup> and 10<sup>th</sup> centuries, Muslim rule was, in general, tolerant of other monotheistic faiths, and even polytheists could publically claim to be Muslims and practice in secret. Most of the Kindred took this route. What converts or embraces there were were rare enough that there was no need for a Covenant, and Muslim vampires worked out what it meant to be a Muslim vampire on their own individual terms.<br /> In the 10<sup>th</sup> century, two trends converged. The more tolerant era of Muslim governance came to an end, requiring actual and meaningful conversion, and enough Muslims were being embraced that the need for a Muslim covenant arose. A new set of sources were unearthed, rejected verses written in vitae-infused blood on human shoulder-blades, (since long lost) that purported to contain passages of the Qur\u2019an that were not accepted due to lack of corroboration, yet they clearly seemed to refer to the vampiric condition.<br /> The verses, known collectively as \u201cAyat al-Kasuuf\u201d or Verses of the Eclipse for the motifs of eclipses that run through them, speak of a people, \u201cA brotherhood hidden amongst you\u201d. \u201cNever will the light\u2019s touch reach them / unless I remove the lights.\u201d They are the \u201chidden shield against that which would harm you / against which I have given you your only recourse.\u201d The verses also make reference to a \u201ctax\u201d that the brotherhood will place upon the people, and that the people will fear them and not know them for what they are.<br /> From lines in these verses, the Covenant drew it\u2019s name. They are normally known as \u201cal-Dara\u2019 al-Khafi\u201d, the Hidden Shield, but their followers are called \u201cIkhwan al-Makhfiun\u201d, the Hidden Brothers, or just \u201cAl-Makhfiun\u201d, The Hidden, for short. They call all vampires \u201cAhl al-Kasuuf\u201d, the People of the Eclipse.<br /> They believe their purpose is to protect people against the Shaitan, the evil Genies who follow Iblis, the Devil. The Shaitan are incorporeal Genies who seek to tempt faithful Muslims from the straight path. Unlike the Lance, who seek to become monsters in order to keep others in line, the Hidden Shield first seeks to balance themselves against the Beast before turning their efforts outwards, in line with a verse that says \u201cOnly those who have defeated the Shaitain (of the self/inside/interior/already) can fight them (successfully/outside/made flesh)\u201d (The verse sometimes varies, this is one of the most debated lines in the Covenant).<br /> There are various factions of the Hidden Shield that hold various beliefs, in part because the texts that make up the Verses of the Eclipse are not wholly agreed upon. Most agree that one must follow the Qur\u2019an unless the Ayat al-Kasuuf differs from the Qur\u2019an, but some say that the Ayat al-Kasuuf overrides the entire Qur\u2019an, because just as the Qur\u2019an was directed towards mortals and Jinn so the Ayat al-Kasuuf were directed towards the Kindred. The latter group is a tiny minority, however.<br /> The larger division is based on a question of purpose. It is accepted in the Covenant that vampires exist to protect mortals, and that in return they draw a tax of blood, yet it is debated exactly what they protect mortals FROM. Some say that they fight only supernatural threats. Some say that they fight only other vampires outside of the Covenant, draugr and others who prey on humans in unacceptable ways. Some say that they must protect mortals from other mortal groups who seek to harm society. A handful say that they must protect individual mortals from themselves! A second question asks WHO do they protect? Do they protect all mortals, or just Muslims? Do they protect only pious Muslims? A third question asks WHO is ALLOWED to protect? Must the Makhfiun completely overcome their own beast to join the good fight? Are they allowed to be imperfect monsters? Or, as a few say, is it allowable to USE the beast in order to better protect the people...<br /> <br /> WHAT CAPABILITIES DO I GIVE THEM?<br /> I\u2019m thinking a set of unique Devotions based on the more common Disciplines, possibly combined with ritualistic prayer? I need to look over the rules again, and maybe get my hands on Secrets of the Covenants. So the sorcery of the covenant must be a subtle thing, something that is internal to the vampire not external that they invoke, something subtle not flashy, something meant to strengthen the self not awe others. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:36:03-07:00","id":872280,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Tivchayim</span><br /> The Undying Path</div> <br /> <i>Fiction blurb</i><br /> <br /> <b>You want to join the covenant because:</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Big Picture:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Our Practices</b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames</b><br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:</b><br /> <br /> <b>When we are in power:</b><br /> <br /> <b>When we are in trouble:<br /> <br /> Covenant Advantages / merits:</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:42:00-07:00","id":872451,"title":"","content":"Your choice of name for the jewish covenant is not good. If you have an idea for a name in english, I can translate it for you.<br /> <br /> Currently it means more &quot;Quality of life&quot; than &quot;Undying Path&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:46:59-07:00","id":878271,"title":"","content":"I can see the differences between human Christianity and The Lance, but what is the difference for the Muslim one? For instance under Sharia there is only three choices for non-muslims(Convert, Submit and pay the tax or die). Would this carry over into a vampire setting? This is just one example off the top of my head. I think a Jewish one might be just as hard to translate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:55:39-07:00","id":878415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=878271#post878271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the differences between human Christianity and The Lance, but what is the difference for the Muslim one? For instance under Sharia there is only three choices for non-muslims(Convert, Submit and pay the tax or die). Would this carry over into a vampire setting? This is just one example off the top of my head. I think a Jewish one might be just as hard to translate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having lived in Abu Dhabi for three years (as an atheist I might add), having dated a Muslim for almost three years (two of which overlapped with Abu Dhabi), and having studied Muslim history for well on a decade, I can tell you from personal experience that this is not the case. I understand the textual basis from which you are drawing, but it is a vast oversimplification that negates centuries of tradition, cultural conflux, and multicultural nation-building that has created other ways of dealing with other faiths, both those that fall within the Ahl al-Kitab and those who do not.<br /> <br /> Also, when creating a Muslim covenant, can we please acknowledge that &quot;Shariah Law&quot; isn't a unified body? Shariah is religious law, but there many ways in which that body of law gets interpreted. You can see a full listing <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Islamic_schools_and_branches\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Long story short, there are many different types of rational that can be used to determine precedence, different Hadith that are considered valid, different ways in which humanity's rational nature can be used to interpret law, and different individuals who have socio-legal-religious authority. It's actually an extremely diverse field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 04-30-2016, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:32:42-07:00","id":898952,"title":"","content":"Any covenant inspired by a real life religion will be faced with problems because the real life religion is far from a unified philosophy or dogma, just like christianity. Islam has the Shia/Sunni schism and countless variations of muslim faith inside those two larger entities, some that are considered close to or outright heretical and non-muslim by other faiths. A really satisfactory covenant would demand some extensive knowledge of the targeted religion and its history (cause the covenant that sprout from it could very well be inherited from ideas that are considered prehistoric nowadays)<br /> <br /> That said, one can imagine a general look for it and some ideas.<br /> <br /> For example, if one would want to imagine a jewish lancea sanctum :<br /> <br /> I would drop the longinus stuff right off the bat because who cares about Jesus, really. Judaism has a devil-like figure in various forms. One of them is an &quot;accuser&quot;, which, if I understand broadly, is basically an agent of god who's supposed to tempt man to sin and turn away from god to test their faith. Basically, he's god's bad cop (which is no small feat considering how ruthless old testament god can be) and not a opposer of god (at least not in this version).<br /> <br /> So basically, they would work kinda the same as the Lancea et Sanctum, messing with humans to see if they're worthy. They wouldn't be bound to the human faith because they're not human, they're the tool of the accuser and while they do evil shit, in the end, they serve the grand scheme of god.<br /> <br /> So how would they get along with the Lancea ? Well, they could work together considering they pretty much do the same thing. The Lancea could also see them as dirty demon worshippers since they serve the &quot;devil&quot;. Seeing they both use theban sorcery, they could see it as a sign that they are on the same mission and tolerate each other's existence (&quot;god works in mysterious ways, sometimes, it's best not to question things too much, and if they really are on god's side, they may end up joining the true faith enventually&quot;), especially faced with really unholy stuff like the Circle of the Crone, or they could accuse each other of usurping their holy powers. That woudl probably depend on the domains, who's in charge of each group locally and what bigger rivals they may have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, I'd be also interested in other non judeo/christian/muslim religion themed covenant using theban sorcery, cause the Lancea Sanctum didn't invent it, they inherited it from egypt or something. What if it also traveled to India and a cult of Shiva worshippers using their own variant of theban sorcery. Their philosophy would be to prepare the world for it's eventual destruction by Shiva, restarting the cycle of creation. In hinduism (again, broadly, I'm not a specialist and hinduism is awfully complicated and not a monolithic faith), Brahma creates the world, Vishnu tends to it and Shiva destroys it once it's expiration date has come. Those vampires could slowly spread corruption, making the world a worse place to hasten it's destruction and the creation of a better world.<br /> <br /> Actually, with how complex hinduism is, with various gods having several aspects that may or may not overlap to an extend depending on who you ask, I could see some pretty interesting dynamic between a Lancea-like covenant and a hindu Circle of the Crone (that could worship Kali or some of the many many demons of hinduism), seeing each other as another aspect of themselves, being careful to not mix, struggling against each other because that is the way things should be but somehow acknowledging each other as a necessary part of the world and so, not wanting to truly eradicate each other. They'd be more like in an eternal ritual war, with the occasionnal mishaps and excess it could bring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:19:19-07:00","id":899319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=898952#post898952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Judaism has a devil-like figure in various forms. One of them is an &quot;accuser&quot;, which, if I understand broadly, is basically an agent of god who's supposed to tempt man to sin and turn away from god to test their faith. Basically, he's god's bad cop (which is no small feat considering how ruthless old testament god can be) and not a opposer of god (at least not in this version).</div> </div> </div> </div>This... isn't really accurate.<br /> <br /> Before the Babylonian exile, HaSatan as referenced to an angel is best idiomatically translated as &quot;the devil's advocate.&quot; HaSatan is presented as the angel responsible for testing the things the Lord created to see if they were &quot;good.&quot; HaSatan only serves the role of directly influencing humans in the book of Job to test the strength of Job's faith. This is not because HaSatan's job is to tempt and test, but because tempting and testing Job was the way to fulfill HaSatan's role to test the Lord's claim of the goodness of Job's faith. HaSatan has a role among the divine host that is not meant to impart any idea that humans are inherent need of supernatural temptation (the Torah is pretty clear we do just fine screwing things up without external influence).<br /> <br /> During the Babylonian and Persian periods, Judaism had a cultural mixing with Zoroastrianism. Zorosastrian dualism lead to an association of HaSatan with the negative forces of darkness. By the Second Temple period, this lead to a schismatic belief in the angel of Sataniel, who is the most direct precursor to the Christian concept of Satan. Sataniel is portrayed as the former highest of the Grigori, who fell from grace and became a force of temptation; and a leader of the Children of Darkness in the final battles.<br /> <br /> Rabbinic Judaism soundly rejected the externalized evil of Sataniel; especially given it's rather direct inspiration from another religion's metaphysical ideology. Early Rabbinic Judaism took the position that while evil spirits exist for any number of reasons, the concept of angels falling from grace to become challengers of the Lord's authority as heretical. Instead the Rabbinic philosophy focused on the concepts of Yetzer HaRa, and Yetzer HaTov: the inclinations to selfishness and selflessness (though more commonly translated as bad and good). All people have both, and must find a balance between them as either in the extreme has negative consequences, and both have important positive things for us to draw on. This strongly focuses on evil actions being the result of choice, not the temptations of evil spirits.<br /> <br /> The problem for a &quot;Jewish&quot; LeS like Covenant is that the only real analog is Sataniel, but Jews have spent the last 2,000 years treating that schism as part of proto-Christianity. To a Jew raised after the Roman sacking of Jerusalem, being turned into a vampire and being presented the options of the LeS or a Sataniel &quot;Jewish&quot; based Covenant would see two things that are essentially the same with a bit for different flair. Modern Jews would be especially skeptical due to groups like Jews of Jesus creating a sense that Christian based groups trying to convert Jews will hide themselves in Jewish terminology to disguise their intentions.<br /> <br /> Basically, this idea only really makes sense as an independent Covenant from the LeS for a limited time in Jewish history during the earliest days of Christianity; and like those splinter groups of Jews, would mostly end up subsumed into the LeS rather than remaining separate.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> If you want to draw and something that can remain more strongly Jewish, the Nephilim are probably a better jumping off point. Children of angels and men (which parallels nicely with how vampires seem to come from the union of people and spiritual entities of specific natures) who were capable of great physical ability, and great potential for both good and evil, but damned for their angelic parents disobedience.<br /> <br /> This could lean more towards a mid-ground between the LeS and the CotC in philosophy. A group of vampires that see their state as both cursed and blessed at the same time, calling on them to seek redemption and a natural place in the world to use their powers to uplift great men, while tearing down evil ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T13:52:12-07:00","id":899356,"title":"","content":"Isn't that Mastema, though? Wouldn't the Lance identify with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T14:51:07-07:00","id":899425,"title":"","content":"Mastema and HaSatan and Sataniel overlap a lot in the texts we have from the Essene schism from Rabbinic Judaism. With the Essene stressing the conflict of light/dark (with the probable influence of Zoroastrianism), a lot of things that were previously more general terms for bad things were personified into fallen angels of various dangers to humanity. It's not clear how much these things were meant to be aspects and different names for the same entity, or meant to be a host of entities.<br /> <br /> The Essene dualism heavily influenced early Christian metaphysics though, and are responsible for the vast majority of Bibilical demonic archetypes the LeS uses to inspire their ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:08:44-07:00","id":899599,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the details and The nephilim are a pretty good idea, although, yeah, like you said, it might be more in line with the Circle's creed. You're right, especially if the covenant has to mirror the modern time religion. I wonder, though. The LeS has some pretty archaic aspects compared to modern catholicism. I mean, the idea that a loving god would actively send monsters to fuck with mortals so that they'd fall in line would seem pretty messed up to most christians (barring fundamentalists and hate groups). For a catholic the Pope never said &quot;be a good christian or the local ventrue bishop will dominate you into beating up old ladies&quot; (sure, the pope acknowledges exorcism as something that is, but demons are supposed to be actual bad guys), and the Malleus Maleficarum definitely has no way of seeing the LeS as a pro-christian group, more like a dreadful deformation of christian beliefs.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while a figure like Hasatan is pretty much abandonned by modern day jewish faith, I could see vampires that keep working with principles they would attach to it (or another figure altogether, the LeS references some angel named amoniel which WW came up with for the occasion). Just because the main human religion doesn't recognize it anymore doesn't mean it doesn't exist. After all, the masquerade being one of the few universal rules of vampires, maybe those particular angels/beings/infrastructures were written off to ensure that the masquerade would hold (hell, like I'm trying to shoehorn things, you could easily imagine a bunch of vampires familiar with the LeS that would try to adapt it to another set of beliefs and rationnalize stuff so it would fit). In the case of a Hasatan themed group, then, they might focus on testing things via negative action because that's mostly what vampires are able to do. To test things another way, they'd figure there are other beings or tools they aren't aware of because it's not their place to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:23:48-07:00","id":899618,"title":"","content":"From my point of view, Lancea Sanctumism is as different from Christianity as Christianity is from Judaism. It just shares a lot of trappings.<br /> <br /> Both LS and Christians have the story of Cavalry and Jesus death, but Christianity and Judaism both have the story of Genesis and no one is saying they are the same. <br /> <br /> A lot of key Christian beliefs are missing from LS theology. I get the LS has reasons why they don't apply (they are damned and all) but the fact that they think a lot of the rules don't apply to them make it a very different religion.<br /> <br /> So why do I bring this up? I think the key thing of making a new Covenant is that while it should have the trappings of Judaism or Islam, it needs to have beliefs that are radically different from both the religion you are baseing it on AND from the LS. If it shares the same goals as the LS (wolves among the sheep), I don't see it as a large enough change to make it a new covenant, at that point, just slap on a new name, priests are called rabbis, come up with a new prophet and be done with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T18:38:37-07:00","id":899631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=899618#post899618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my point of view, Lancea Sanctumism is as different from Christianity as Christianity is from Judaism. It just shares a lot of trappings.<br /> <br /> Both LS and Christians have the story of Cavalry and Jesus death, but Christianity and Judaism both have the story of Genesis and no one is saying they are the same.<br /> <br /> A lot of key Christian beliefs are missing from LS theology. I get the LS has reasons why they don't apply (they are damned and all) but the fact that they think a lot of the rules don't apply to them make it a very different religion.<br /> <br /> So why do I bring this up? I think the key thing of making a new Covenant is that while it should have the trappings of Judaism or Islam, it needs to have beliefs that are radically different from both the religion you are baseing it on AND from the LS. If it shares the same goals as the LS (wolves among the sheep), I don't see it as a large enough change to make it a new covenant, at that point, just slap on a new name, priests are called rabbis, come up with a new prophet and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get your point about just making cosmetic changes if there isn't a big difference, but just swapping priest for Rabbis or adding a vampire Prophet isn't really a solution either. An Islamic &quot;wolves amongst sheep&quot; looks very different from a Christian which looks very different from a Hebrew one. In fact, I'm writing an Islamic (specifically Ibadi/Kharijite) bloodline that hates LeS, the Iblic Creed, and the mortals in Daesh (ISIL, but I call them Daesh like the Arab world does because they want to be called ISIL and hate being called Daesh) all with an equally burning passion.<br /> <br /> My point is, if you are actually using the beliefs of Muslims, Jews, and Christians to inform the way their respective Kindred communities have evolved, then you will get those massive differences that make them unique. The root concept may be similar, but they will end up in vastly different places. The only way you that a Muslim covenant looks like a Christian one is if you do name swaps form LeS. If you take the time to study the history, philosophy, and government of the group you are trying to write about, the differences will come.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Actually, instead of just babbling about how different the cultures and mindsets are, here's a suggestion: Read Chapter 1 of God's Rule: Government and Islam by Patricia Crone. It makes it abundantly clear the religious and political differences between the Christian and Muslim views of the Garden of Eden, Sin, and political legitimacy. From there, it would be easy to see how the Iblic Creed would end up extremely different from LeS","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 05-25-2016, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T05:34:06-07:00","id":899941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=899631#post899631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get your point about just making cosmetic changes if there isn't a big difference, but just swapping priest for Rabbis or adding a vampire Prophet isn't really a solution either. An Islamic &quot;wolves amongst sheep&quot; looks very different from a Christian which looks very different from a Hebrew one. In fact, I'm writing an Islamic (specifically Ibadi/Kharijite) bloodline that hates LeS, the Iblic Creed, and the mortals in Daesh (ISIL, but I call them Daesh like the Arab world does because they want to be called ISIL and hate being called Daesh) all with an equally burning passion.<br /> <br /> My point is, if you are actually using the beliefs of Muslims, Jews, and Christians to inform the way their respective Kindred communities have evolved, then you will get those massive differences that make them unique. The root concept may be similar, but they will end up in vastly different places. The only way you that a Muslim covenant looks like a Christian one is if you do name swaps form LeS. If you take the time to study the history, philosophy, and government of the group you are trying to write about, the differences will come.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT</b>: Actually, instead of just babbling about how different the cultures and mindsets are, here's a suggestion: Read Chapter 1 of God's Rule: Government and Islam by Patricia Crone. It makes it abundantly clear the religious and political differences between the Christian and Muslim views of the Garden of Eden, Sin, and political legitimacy. From there, it would be easy to see how the Iblic Creed would end up extremely different from LeS</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote a long response to this but deicded that it was to negative and I am mostly interested and sceptical (in a good sense) in what you will come up with.<br /> <br /> I am actually on the same page as you that there are all different, I thought I was clear in my second paragraph. I think you may have focused to much on my last sentence to the exclusion of the preceding seven ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:09:09-07:00","id":899960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=899941#post899941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wrote a long response to this but deicded that it was to negative and I am mostly interested and sceptical (in a good sense) in what you will come up with.<br /> <br /> I am actually on the same page as you that there are all different, I thought I was clear in my second paragraph. I think you may have focused to much on my last sentence to the exclusion of the preceding seven ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. I'm just vehemently against doing a name swap, since each religion is unique and you can't do name swaps there, so each covalent should also be unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:17:10-07:00","id":899965,"title":"","content":"A good starting point for a Jewish based Covenant might be Leviticus 17:14. Please correct me if wrong, but my understanding of 'anyone who partakes of blood will be cut off' means a spiritual cut off. Tying in with the Nephilim suggestion, maybe a Covenant formed with Jewish vampires struggling to understand why they were saddled with a curse that (potentially) would keep them forever spiritually impure/cut off from Gd. They decided they were the descendants of the original Nephilim, some of whom escaped the purge of the Biblical Flood.<br /> <br /> Since Gd promised not to destroy the world again, drinking blood, sunlight, et al, are the ways Gd set the surviving Nephilim apart.<br /> <br /> Instead of Theban Sorcery, they could have something similar to Coils, because they see their state not as a curse, but as a struggle to be overcome so they can once again be spiritually clean and not cut off from Gd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11149,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","user":"PJ123","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T06:32:59-07:00","id":899977,"title":"","content":"One thing I notice in this discussion is that there are a lot of people who are treating Christianity as some monolithic organization. There are sweeping differences between, say, a snake charmer tent-preacher revivalist church and a Catholic study group. And the vampire versions of these are going to be just as varied as the mortal ones. They have different culture and beliefs that will create vast changes in how they appear.<br /> <br /> So, when people are trying to make comparisons from an Islamic or Jewish vampire to a Christian one (or Longinian), I have to ask - &quot;What <i>kind?&quot; </i><br /> <br /> The whole point of this thread is to hear exactly how these different groups should be different. We've heard some good things about how Jewish and Islamic humans in real life are different. So, how does that apply to vampires now? Would we have complete rejection of the &quot;wolves among sheep&quot; doctrine? If so, what would we replace it with? What's the daily life like?<br /> <br /> EDIT - So far, all I see is difference in history. I personally consider history swaps to be nothing more than cosmetic changes. Someone early on mentioned that a Muslim covenant would protect people from evil spirits - the Lance does the same thing as well, so that's not a notable difference. And it also doesn't touch on the night-to-night life of the vampire in question. I dont' think that Covenants are defined by how they treat mortals, I think they're defined by what part they take in the Danse Macabre and the All Night Society. Even if you want to argue that they are defined by mortal treatment in part, lets hear more about how these new covenants would take part in the Danse. The central them of Vampire is What do they do? You're a monster now, how do you live your unlife? Lets answer that.<br /> <br /> ***************************<br /> <br /> Another thing I think that should be mentioned. Theban Sorcery, by its nature, is not blood magic or any kind of magical rituals. They're called <i>dark miracles</i> specifically because they channel miracles from a divine being, whereas Cruac uses the inner goddess of the vampire. Theban has &quot;specific god X&quot; themed spells, while Cruac has &quot;vampire themed magic&quot; untied to any specific religion. We have Catholic themed miracles currently. If we had an Egyptian user of Theban, we'd have Ra-themed magic effects. Basically, if Theban had Styles like Cruac did, we'd have Catholic style, Egyptian style, Hindu style, etc. Right now, these styles merely manifest in the theme of the miracles the vampire learns. Its arguable that a Theban Sorcerer can even learn a different style, since who grants these powers might change.<br /> <br /> So, given the above, should Jewish and Islamic vampires channel the power of God through miracles as well? And, if so, what should the rituals be like? If not, then what should the covenant advantage do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T10:13:38-07:00","id":900157,"title":"","content":"Jewish and Islamic in-life vampires are going to have trouble thinking that they can channel divine miracles through their cursed state. Both religions largely hold that such powers were lost with the cessation of divinely anointed prophets to channel them, and the idea that magical blood would allow access to such blessings is a huge leap to try to make.<br /> <br /> The Nephilim option is one way to help that, but it ends up as noted somewhere between Theban and Cruac. It's channeling an external source of miracles, through an internal divine link.<br /> <br /> Another way to is have them go full demonologist. Jewish and Islamic mythology has a lot more room for &quot;spirit pact&quot; style approaches that are still channel miracles from a supernaturally potent being, just not divine ones. Hermetic style bindings could be a fluffed take on Theban, or a separate Discipline... an Islamic way would probably go closer to a Sufi variant on Cruac in style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:16:26-07:00","id":900346,"title":"","content":"Channeling miralces have nothing to do with a cursed state. You're asking for the intercession of God or an angel, basically - after all, that's literally the definition of miracle. (And, for that reason, you can't make a miracle by your own internal power; that's not divine intercession.) And all three Abrahamic branches include members who pray to God to intervene on their behalf; miracles are still a thing in all religions. You are not making an argument that Christians wouldn't as well, and yet we have the LeS and Theban. Remember that we're not talking about human religions that happen to have vampires in them. We're talking about covenants - organizations that are built by vampires for vampires, and cater to the dark nature of vampires. These are <i>encouraged</i> to have systems of beliefs that deviate from what we humans have. So, arbitrarily saying that a group can't have such things makes no real sense. Its an unnecessary restriction. I can understand wanting a different style of powers, but arguing that miracles are a not a modern thing for the Jewish or Muslim? That's not true.<br /> <br /> <br /> Either way, when it comes to power design, one of the most important things are that they are <i>active</i>. Powers in vampire aren't passive. They're active, they create / progress stories, and often highly coercive. They are dark, and not beneficial for humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:49:55-07:00","id":900463,"title":"","content":"Wow. Great educational discussion, awesome! I love you guys.<br /> <br /> For my two cents, knowing not nearly as much as I should about either Judaism or Islam, is along these lines:<br /> <br /> For me, the fundamental defining factor of the Lancea et Sanctum is the idea of the sacrifice of Jesus Christ. According to Christian belief, Jesus was sent to atone for the sins of Man by giving His life. But God sent no savior to the Kindred, they are still damned, inherently sinful creatures, arguably more than humans before they are baptized and given the forgiveness of Jesus Christ Our Lord And Savior. That's the fundamental difference from which everything else spreads. The Sanctum ask why are we still damned, then come up with an answer, then come up with codes of behavior based on that answer. Why are we still Damned? God must <i>want</i> us to be monsters? Then how should we act? Like monsters, <i>duh</i>.<br /> <br /> So, what I would do is identify the &quot;point of separation&quot; for both Judaism and Islam when it comes to God's relations to humans versus vampires. It was mentioned earlier that Mohammed was God's &quot;final word,&quot; so to speak, and thus a Muslim Covenant couldn't be based on any writings before or after Mohammed. But Mohammed, like Jesus, was a prophet sent to <i>humanity</i>. Not the Kindred. If the Kindred do not have their own prophet, and the teachings of Mohammed do not apply to them, then they're pretty much stuck in the same situation as the Sanctum. . . basically making it up for themselves. If Allah did not send the Kindred a Prophet, why? What are they supposed to do with His lack of divine guidance? How do they fit into Allah's grand plan, and what can they do to aid it? I have no answers, since as mentioned I have very little knowledge of Islam, but I think these are the questions that should be asked when creating a Muslim Covenant.<br /> <br /> From what I know of Judaism, one of the fundamental tenets is that the Jewish people are God's chosen. Are vampires made from Jews then &quot;un-chosen,&quot; or are they chosen for something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T17:00:42-07:00","id":900477,"title":"","content":"I think to an extent you're taking the &quot;Covenants are vampire institutions for vampires,&quot; too far. If you want a Jewish or Muslim inspired Covenant like the LeS is for Christianity, it has to be a philosophy that makes sense for vampires that practiced those religions in life would embrace.<br /> <br /> Judaism and Islam absolutely have a concept of miracles. What they don't have is a concept of the continuation of the line of miracle workers. The majority of Christian sects still hold the belief that the faithful can perform miracles via divine supplication. Whether you're talking the Catholic saints, or the charismatic faith healers, it is something Christianity holds to this day as something people can do. Judaism and Islam don't share that belief. Any miracle is part of the divine plan, not the direct intercession based on an individual of great faith's actions.<br /> <br /> Yes, a non-Christian Abrahamic Covenant could be heretical in that fashion, but if you keep doing that, it stops being something that makes sense as a vampire institution that serves the vampire goal of giving Embraced faithful a place and explanation for their unlife. A Jewish based Covenant needs to have the narrative appeal of being something that a pre-Embrace Jew would find solace in as part of finding their purpose in the Danse Macbre. If that Covenant doesn't have a good sale to Jews in terms Jews would appreciate, it doesn't work. If the ways it bucks mainstream Jewish belief don't have a strong path to explain why they do things differently, they can't successfully recruit.<br /> <br /> Theban Sorcery on a philosophic level doesn't make sense to a Jewish or Islamic perspective. There isn't a good bridge between, &quot;in life you didn't believe the power to make supplication for direct divine intercession was still possible, but it totally is to undead monsters.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T18:50:11-07:00","id":900544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900477#post900477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think to an extent you're taking the &quot;Covenants are vampire institutions for vampires,&quot; too far. If you want a Jewish or Muslim inspired Covenant like the LeS is for Christianity, it has to be a philosophy that makes sense for vampires that practiced those religions in life would embrace.<br /> <br /> Judaism and Islam absolutely have a concept of miracles. What they don't have is a concept of the continuation of the line of miracle workers. The majority of Christian sects still hold the belief that the faithful can perform miracles via divine supplication. Whether you're talking the Catholic saints, or the charismatic faith healers, it is something Christianity holds to this day as something people can do. Judaism and Islam don't share that belief. Any miracle is part of the divine plan, not the direct intercession based on an individual of great faith's actions.<br /> <br /> Yes, a non-Christian Abrahamic Covenant could be heretical in that fashion, but if you keep doing that, it stops being something that makes sense as a vampire institution that serves the vampire goal of giving Embraced faithful a place and explanation for their unlife. A Jewish based Covenant needs to have the narrative appeal of being something that a pre-Embrace Jew would find solace in as part of finding their purpose in the Danse Macbre. If that Covenant doesn't have a good sale to Jews in terms Jews would appreciate, it doesn't work. If the ways it bucks mainstream Jewish belief don't have a strong path to explain why they do things differently, they can't successfully recruit.<br /> <br /> Theban Sorcery on a philosophic level doesn't make sense to a Jewish or Islamic perspective. There isn't a good bridge between, &quot;in life you didn't believe the power to make supplication for direct divine intercession was still possible, but it totally is to undead monsters.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe most Christians will easily adopt the teachings of Lancea Sanctum. A &quot;good&quot; LS vampire is very different from what a good Christian is.<br /> <br /> I think most Christians after being embraced would think the LS is completely insane, if not completely demonic. They would most likely keep their Christian faith for years if not decades (even if this eventually fails to fulfill them like it did in life).<br /> <br /> The LS preaches against mercy (Blessed are the merciful). The LS preaches that God needs your help to keep the faithful in line (this is Pride). The mere fact that they believe their job is to save people by driving them to the church via fear instead of faith in Jesus is a major departure. One is suppose to do unto others, they don't. You should remove the plank of wood in your own eye, before you remove the speck from someone elses, they don't hold that to be valid for themselves. Christians don't mention vampires often anymore but when they do, they are not servants of heavan but servants of hell. The church traditionally destroys vampires. LS members do not believe their sins can be forgiven, for Christians, God forgives all. Catholic and Orthodox sects believe that Longinus was a martyr for the church, his body was a holy relic and that rather than curse him, Jesus' blood healed his blindness. I get why LS theology works for vampires and why vampires are exempt from these rules in LS doctrine, but this is extremely different from Christian dogma and doctrine and I think people underestimate how disconcerting this would be for people that were faithful in life to adjust to this opposite point of view. The bottom has dropped out from becoming a vampire, they need to cling to something and turning your back on all your beliefs is another huge loss.<br /> <br /> In short, I don't think its fair to say that the philosophy (theology really) is one that living Christians would easily accept (although I will admit that some new vampires will for a number of reasons)<br /> <br /> I feel like I keep making this arguement, can someone please explain to me how LS theology/belief is like Christianity theology/belief in general (examples would be useful)? I get the Jesus on the cross part, but they depart pretty hard outside of saying it happened. I also get that their rituals are similar but I always assumed that was mimicry. Help me out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:18:46-07:00","id":900559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900544#post900544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">LS members do not believe their sins can be forgiven, for Christians, God forgives all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise some really good points, but here is the main point of divergence. Jesus' sacrifice abolished the sins <i>of humanity</i>. Vampires are not human. God sent no Savior to abolish their sin. They are still doomed by Original Sin, and all the other sins they commit since then. By a lot of entries in both Testaments of the Bible, simply being a vampire is an inherently sinful life. They drink human blood, are exempt from death and judgement, etc. The rules laid down in Christianity just do not apply to them, so they require a different set of rules to define what is, to them, living in accordance with God's will. While a person turned into a vampire could try and cling to their Christian beliefs, they'd have to throw out large chunks of Biblical proscriptions to do so. Instead, the Lancea et Sanctum says that God has a plan for all beings, vampires included, and these are what are required of one who is a &quot;proper&quot; vampire in God's eyes. And that involves being a complete monster, because that's how God made you. Just as God made humans to be innocent before they were tempted by Original Sin, and humanity as a whole strives to reach that state once again (according to most Christian dogma). That could actually be a powerful recruiting tool for the Sanctum. A Christian turned into a vampire hears the Sanctum dogma, declares them insane because it goes against what Christianity stands for, and declares they won't join and cling to their Christian faith and human-centric rules. Then the Sanctum recruiter points out all the ways in which their very existence violates the rules and proscriptions in the Bible, and states that it's simply impossible for a vampire to live as a good Christian. Thus, God clearly intended for there to be two sets of rules, one for humans, which He had codified and written down, and one for vampires, which remains largely secret. The Sanctum knows that secret. Would you like to know more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T20:49:34-07:00","id":900640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900559#post900559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You raise some really good points, but here is the main point of divergence. Jesus' sacrifice abolished the sins <i>of humanity</i>. Vampires are not human. God sent no Savior to abolish their sin. They are still doomed by Original Sin, and all the other sins they commit since then. By a lot of entries in both Testaments of the Bible, simply being a vampire is an inherently sinful life. They drink human blood, are exempt from death and judgement, etc. The rules laid down in Christianity just do not apply to them, so they require a different set of rules to define what is, to them, living in accordance with God's will. While a person turned into a vampire could try and cling to their Christian beliefs, they'd have to throw out large chunks of Biblical proscriptions to do so. Instead, the Lancea et Sanctum says that God has a plan for all beings, vampires included, and these are what are required of one who is a &quot;proper&quot; vampire in God's eyes. And that involves being a complete monster, because that's how God made you. Just as God made humans to be innocent before they were tempted by Original Sin, and humanity as a whole strives to reach that state once again (according to most Christian dogma). That could actually be a powerful recruiting tool for the Sanctum. A Christian turned into a vampire hears the Sanctum dogma, declares them insane because it goes against what Christianity stands for, and declares they won't join and cling to their Christian faith and human-centric rules. Then the Sanctum recruiter points out all the ways in which their very existence violates the rules and proscriptions in the Bible, and states that it's simply impossible for a vampire to live as a good Christian. Thus, God clearly intended for there to be two sets of rules, one for humans, which He had codified and written down, and one for vampires, which remains largely secret. The Sanctum knows that secret. Would you like to know more?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not saying your view is wrong and it can't happen the way you describe, I just think thats how people always think of it: devout Christian in life, must be a Lancea Sanctum member in death. I think its limiting to always draw that line as its more complex than that. On the other hand, to support your point, a lot of Christians aren't as much into the theology/belief side of the religion as much as they are into other parts of the experience and they may be much more interested in LS doctrine.<br /> <br /> By the by, I really like your recruitment pitch, I am going to steal it.<br /> <br /> Regarding reaching a state as they were prior to original sin, I don't think that's particularly Christian. Christinaity's take (and I admit there is a lot of variation) is that you are born a sinner, your natural state is to sin, you should try not to sin, but you will sin eventually. That's okay though because you will be forgiven if you ask, just try not to do it again, although you will. Thats why priests and reverands often declare themselves sinners.<br /> <br /> My original post was meant to refute the statement that any covenant that is Islamic orJudaic in nature needs to be not to far from the religions beliefs of those religions by showing that LS beliefs aren't very close to Christian beliefs, not state that no good Christian would ever become a member of the LS. EDIT: That being said, that goal could easily be lost on someone who actual read the first sentence of my post and assumed that what I said was what I was trying to say, doh.<br /> <br /> And finally, great conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","user":"Joboo","date":". 05-26-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:38:30-07:00","id":900669,"title":"","content":"An important detail. LS was originslly a Jewish covenant, the Sanctum. They were a small faction of the roman Collegia Peregrina, but around 1st Century they opened their ranks to other marginal faiths from the Empire. The Longinians (the Lancea) were one of those faiths and about 3rd-4rth Century they were thecdominant faction and dplintered from the Collegia.<br /> <br /> About the muslim covenant, an idea I thought about its origin could be a Sanctified who hears about the teachings of Muhammad and converted to Islam, trying to adapt it to vampire condition. May be he was an exiled Sanctified from Arabia, may be even hearing durectly from Muhammad. Or may be he was an scholar from Antiochy, Jerusalem or Alexandria and converted to Islam after the conquest.<br /> Another possibility could be a muslim imam Embraced by a Sanctified, who tried to combine the preachings of Muhammad with the teachings of his sire (and maybe claiming having an angelic visitation not accepted by &quot;christian&quot; Sanctified).<br /> In either way, that could justify the use of Theban Sorcery by the Banu Shaitan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 05-27-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:40:12-07:00","id":900673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants#post872276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this has come up several times. A number of people want to see a muslim-based covenant for a number of reasons. And, despite no real calls for it, there should be consideration for jewish faith as well - jews aren't christian-lite, and we should not treat them as such.<br /> <br /> So, I'm going to write out an outline for the two, and people who are interested in creating these homebrew covenants can suggest adding things in. The Iblic Creed / Benu Shaitan an Dammitic creed were written with the eye to become Lancea Creeds, so don't feel constrained by that. Lets hear all ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT - names are merely placeholders, so feel free to make suggestions to change those as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If there is a Jewish covenant, I would suggest making the Daeva a noticeable part of it. Succubi are derived from Hebrew mythology, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T22:58:46-07:00","id":900715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900640#post900640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not saying your view is wrong and it can't happen the way you describe, I just think thats how people always think of it: devout Christian in life, must be a Lancea Sanctum member in death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's how people are thinking. It's more of a case that the LeS has to represent a reasonable path for a devout Christian in life. There should be other paths to the Covenant, but they're less problematic to the core concepts and themes. An atheist that's Embraced, and upon realizing how much supernatural craziness is out in the world opts to find religion and joins the LeS is perfectly fine as well, but that character doesn't have to resolve the cognitive dissonance of Christianity vs. Longinism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My original post was meant to refute the statement that any covenant that is Islamic orJudaic in nature needs to be not to far from the religions beliefs of those religions by showing that LS beliefs aren't very close to Christian beliefs, not state that no good Christian would ever become a member of the LS. </div> </div> </div>This wasn't my point though. It isn't that a Jewish or Islamic Covenant needs to be &quot;closer&quot; to actual practice than the LeS is to Christianity. But that the bridge between the religion and the Covenant needs to make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T03:04:20-07:00","id":900803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900477#post900477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think to an extent you're taking the &quot;Covenants are vampire institutions for vampires,&quot; too far. If you want a Jewish or Muslim inspired Covenant like the LeS is for Christianity, it has to be a philosophy that makes sense for vampires that practiced those religions in life would embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div> Uhhh, no, it doesn't. The LetS and CotC put a lie to that statement. The entire concept of taking a Humanity breaking point for joining a covenant puts a lie to that statement.<br /> <br /> Ignoring that these are primarily vampire institutions is the trap here. Carthians are the notable exception, specifically because they are designed as the exception, and even then their practices focus on making life better for vampires and not humans. New covenants need to make sense from a vampire perspective above all else, not a mortal one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What they don't have is a concept of the continuation of the line of miracle workers. </div> </div> </div> They don't have a concept of the continuation of <i>prophets</i>, which is an entirely different matter. Prophets are those who reveal the will of God. It has nothing to do with the continuation of mystic practices in those religions, which rely on divine intervention. Islam at certain points in history were well renowned for their numerology and a large number of other theurgical practices. Jewish superstitions include amulets with scriptures in them for protections through divine intercession.<br /> <br /> If you feel there's better ways to refect these covenants, go for it. Jewish and Islamic mysticism might reflect better with different mechanics. But history shows us that workings are a thing in these religions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Theban Sorcery on a philosophic level doesn't make sense to a Jewish or Islamic perspective. There isn't a good bridge between, &quot;in life you didn't believe the power to make supplication for direct divine intercession was still possible, but it totally is to undead monsters.&quot; </div> </div> </div> Jewish and Islamic prayers include petitions for the Divine's help as well as blessings. Its part of these religions. So, I'm going to disagree here as well. It tends to be highly ritualized, but its a thing. The point is that, while there might be better mechanics and systems out there, there's no philosophic disagreement here, as you put it.<br /> <br /> And, honestly? You also have to remember that we're on the other side of the Veil now. Magic in the CofD is the occult - the hidden. What was hidden is now revealed to the dead in a way that the living never could. So just because you didn't expect something on one side of the veil doesn't mean that it doesn't exist on the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-27-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T03:41:28-07:00","id":900812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900544#post900544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I keep making this arguement, can someone please explain to me how LS theology/belief is like Christianity theology/belief in general (examples would be useful)? I get the Jesus on the cross part, but they depart pretty hard outside of saying it happened. I also get that their rituals are similar but I always assumed that was mimicry. Help me out.</div> </div> </div> </div> You've basically hit the nail on its head. The LetS only has superficial similarities to Catholism / parts of Christianity. It is mimicry. However, that is more than enough for most people, both in terms of players and in-game characters. Form follows function - our minds are wired to accept things that are similar to what we remember, and superficial similarities are highly effective in making things palatable when they'd otherwise be disgusting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900640#post900640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding reaching a state as they were prior to original sin, I don't think that's particularly Christian. Christinaity's take (and I admit there is a lot of variation) is that you are born a sinner, your natural state is to sin, you should try not to sin, but you will sin eventually. That's okay though because you will be forgiven if you ask, just try not to do it again, although you will. Thats why priests and reverands often declare themselves sinners.</div> </div> </div> </div> Original sin is a <i>Catholic </i>doctine, not Christian. Its actually considered an alien concept in most denominations.<br /> <br /> Catholicism is not the whole of Christianity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900559#post900559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That could actually be a powerful recruiting tool for the Sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, totally is. Easy answers and a Mission in undeath is a really good hook for the Sanctum. The fun thing is that its designed in a way to ease transition from a human mindset into a vampiric mindset. Don't think like a mortal. Think like an undead predator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900715#post900715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's how people are thinking. It's more of a case that the LeS has to represent a reasonable path for a devout Christian in life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, its not a reasonable path at all. That's exactly the problem. The Lancea Et Sanctum doesn't recruit the faithful that just happen to be Embraced. They seek out <i>sinners</i> to Embrace and draw them in based on guilt and a need for penance (possibly an artificially imposed need via coercive disciplines or more mundane methods of brainwashing). <br /> <br /> The devout generally aren't Embraced. And, if they are, the LetS message is going to fall flat - they didn't do anything to deserve Damnation. Why are they being punished for it? They were Cursed because someone infected them with a mystical disease. It makes no sense.<br /> <br /> Actually, the path of the devout Christian is to wait for the sunrise and martyr themselves so they don't risk hurting others, which will eventually happen. Or join the Ordo Dracul - while the Dragons officially declare seeking Golconda a heresy, the Sworn of the Ladder are completely devoted to that exact detail. When the game says &quot;heresy,&quot; you know that there's a devoted subgroup to doing just that in the covenant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This wasn't my point though. It isn't that a Jewish or Islamic Covenant needs to be &quot;closer&quot; to actual practice than the LeS is to Christianity. But that the bridge between the religion and the Covenant needs to make sense. </div> </div> </div> While the bridge does need to make sense, you also need to consider that we're dealing with non-mainstream people here. Vampire coveants represent the darker aspects of humanity; VtR is all about balancing the Human and Beast, the Pious and the Blasphemous. Yes, Piety and Blasphemy are part of the game - its right there in the beginning of the book. And covenants, as vampire institutions, lean more towards enabling the blasphemous.<br /> <br /> The LetS represents the hypocracy of many Catholics, the guilt and the indulgences, the book burnings and the patriarchal dominion. They draw from the pedophiles and the power abusers. These people are all the dark propaganda of the Inquisition made &quot;real.&quot; These are definitely not mainstream, devout Christians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T04:03:23-07:00","id":900820,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; For me, the fundamental defining factor of the Lancea et Sanctum is the idea of the sacrifice of Jesus Christ. According to Christian belief, Jesus was sent to atone for the sins of Man by giving His life. But God sent no savior to the Kindred, they are still damned, inherently sinful creatures, arguably more than humans before they are baptized and given the forgiveness of Jesus Christ Our Lord And Savior. That's the fundamental difference from which everything else spreads. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> According to Sanctified doctrine, kindred were humans who were damned. The problem with that is that Jesus was the sacrificial lamb to atone for all sins (save one - blasphemy against the Holy Spirit, successful suicide is another arguable point but that's another can of worms) not just the sins of a select group of humans. So if kindred are humans who were damned yet they believed Jesus died for their sins and had accepted him as the messiah yet they didn't commit the unforgivable sin, then why are they being arbitrarily denied entrance into the presence of God? So either the Lancea Sanctum doctrine is fatally flawed about kindred being damned, their definition of damned differs significantly from what most religions consider that state and they are actively preying on those assumptions, or Christianity is a complete and utter sham. I don't see those who were true Christians prior to the embrace accepting that talking point to doctrine so readily, any more than a Jew or Muslim would. Yes there are some caveats that could be tacked onto Sanctified core doctrine, the simplest being that someone being turned into a vampire is an individual's test of faith (like Job, Abraham, Jonah etc.), a form of purgatory to atone for something, or they still have a calling to perform they never fulfilled in life, and not actual damnation, but that is not the normal default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-27-2016, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T09:59:29-07:00","id":901100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900812#post900812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Original sin is a <i>Catholic </i>doctine, not Christian. Its actually considered an alien concept in most denominations.<br /> <br /> Catholicism is not the whole of Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, I guess you know which angle I come at Christianity from.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Orthodoxy and Anglicans does have original sin as well. (combined thats over 58% of Christians, but less in the US). So its an awful lot of Christians, even if its not a universal belief.<br /> <br /> By the by, this conversation makes me realize why so many people were shocked and surprised when the Pope recently called himself a sinner. Its not part of their Christianity.<br /> <br /> I have seen a number of conversations on the topic of LS Christianity over the years and this is the most impressive one I have seen to date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","user":"Joboo","date":". 05-27-2016, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:12:17-07:00","id":901115,"title":"","content":"Ok, I had some bigger responses, but I realize it's not the best idea right now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> I really do want to continue this, but it's getting to the point where I'm feeling like I'm getting goy-splained out. I've been practicing my faith for over 30 years. I have taken over 15 formal academic courses specifically about my religion beyond that.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to put all that to good use to help you make a good Covenant. Right now all I feel I'm getting back is that you don't think I actually understand my own religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:53:33-07:00","id":901219,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts, and warning - I am a pop culture religious student. Taken some myth classes and religious comparisons, but mostly everything I know is second hand or picked up through media. So apologies for anything that seems stupidly inauthentic or out of place. Consider this slightly uninformed brainstorming, really. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... the Rabbinic philosophy focused on the concepts of Yetzer HaRa, and Yetzer HaTov: the inclinations to selfishness and selflessness (though more commonly translated as bad and good). All people have both, and must find a balance between them as either in the extreme has negative consequences, and both have important positive things for us to draw on. This strongly focuses on evil actions being the result of choice, not the temptations of evil spirits. ... This could lean more towards a mid-ground between the LeS and the CotC in philosophy. A group of vampires that see their state as both cursed and blessed at the same time, calling on them to seek redemption and a natural place in the world to use their powers to <i>uplift great men, while tearing down evil ones</i>. </div> </div> </div>This jumped out at me as an interesting take. The Circle and the Lance both have a direct connection to the Humanity Stat in terms of their disciplines. The higher you are, the more Theban you can learn. The lower, the more Cruac. A Covenant that maintains a center-balance (5-6) would be a natural mid-point and could be an interesting mechanic. The more extreme you are either way, the less control you have over your signature discipline.<br /> <br /> There's lots of write-ups on how the Beast as a force is personified and other'ed by different Kindred. I like the idea of a philosophy that takes that same personification and other'ing and applies it equally to the Man. A group that puts the 'Self' between the Man and the Beast, looking at them both as imperfect reflections of the true inner being. Letting either one get out of balance is equally immoral. <br /> <br /> For factions, you could have the inwardly-focused group, that looks mostly internally, personal journeys. Is Kabbalah actually a traditional part of Judaism, or mostly just something the West made up like Yoga? Assuming the former, I can't imagine it would be difficult to base a discipline or set of devotions from it.<br /> <br /> An externally facing faction could also work. One that takes direct action in the world to draw things back down to balance. You could even have subsets there, one subfaction which concentrates on the balance in an individual - pushing the person with low humanity up, or pushing the person with high humanity back down toward the center. Another subset could function on the macro scale, who might step in to counteract the Sanctified when they are in power by allying with the Circle, but if the Circle 'win' and the Lance drops - the group switches sides to keep that balance. (Though now I'm reminded a little of D&amp;D Druids, so that would need some work.)<br /> <br /> As for function in the All Night Society - the quick thought that popped out at me is always having been fascinated with Kosher rules. The restrictions and ritual of it always seemed very interesting, if something I would never buy into personally - even going to Catholic school I never followed fish-only Fridays. But - for the question: <i>What type of True Christian would embrace the Lance</i> - a good answer is one who sees that Theban Sorcerers <i>can actually do miracles</i>. I suspect I would forgive a lot of dogma, would give up being an atheist, if I actually saw miracles first hand. In any case, if those food practices actually had an obvious mystical effect behind them - when applied to the preparation and consumption of blood (like stripping out addictive qualities or Vinculum, or even giving unique buffs or defbuffs for lack of better terms), that gives a reason to fit into the ANS pretty well. People need blood, and blood without traditional risks is valuable.<br /> <br /> Though, I imagine you'd have to be very careful how you treat the subject in terms of blood libel and such. As an outsider I don't feel I'd be able to treat that issue with the appropriate care and understanding it would need, so I'll leave it there for now.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> New thought for the Islamic idea. When speaking of Muhammad as the final and complete prophet, is there any loophole or wiggle room for a previous prophet that, say, still exists because they became immortal?<br /> <br /> Using Wiki, I quickly found the piece on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zechariah_(priest)#In_Islam\" target=\"_blank\">Zecharia</a>. A figure potentially believed to be the guardian of Mary. Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And (Zechariah) said: &quot;O my Lord, my bones decay, my head is white and hoary, yet in calling You, O Lord, I have never been deprived. But I fear my relatives after me; and my wife is barren. So grant me a successor of Your own Who will be heir to me, and heir to the house of Jacob; and make him obedient to You, O Lord </div> </div> </div>I'll note that Vampires are barren, but can still make Childer, regardless of how old they were in life or look in death. A group that sees the creation of Childer as a holy act and a gift from God would also have a place in the All Night Society. Picking up abandoned strays, Revenants, putting a value in the Childe as an expression of faith and/or tradition that could find a middle ground between the Invictus and Carthians, perhaps.<br /> <br /> And yeah, what if one of the pre-Muhammad prophets (or someone who claimed to be) was actually still here to speak. I imagine they wouldn't be able to directly speak on issues Muhammad defined. But what about issues that weren't specifically defined during his time on Earth. Would such a figure have any kind of spiritual authority from the Islamic perspective? <br /> <br /> What if most of the undefined ideas are actually modern ones? That could be an interesting dichotomy, too. Most of the ideas present in the Middle-Ages would have been spoken on by Muhammad, so it could be easier to speak on things like industrialization or computers since there wouldn't be pieces in the Koran or Islamic teaching that directly relate to them.<br /> <br /> /brainstorm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T12:45:26-07:00","id":901284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=901115#post901115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I had some bigger responses, but I realize it's not the best idea right now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a> I really do want to continue this, but it's getting to the point where I'm feeling like I'm getting goy-splained out. I've been practicing my faith for over 30 years. I have taken over 15 formal academic courses specifically about my religion beyond that.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to put all that to good use to help you make a good Covenant. Right now all I feel I'm getting back is that you don't think I actually understand my own religion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had one post that disagreed with your beliefs, which was probably wrong on my part on reflection. After that, though? I've been arguing what I am good at - game design standpoints. <br /> <br /> Most importantly, I think you're focusing on translating mainstream for human organization directly into vampires, and that's something that doesn't work. And, once you're a vampire, we move away from magic being hidden / unavailable to being everywhere. Its a shift in tone and understanding. You literally see angels and spirits and ghosts. I don't think you are taking that into account.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:09:38-07:00","id":901531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=901100#post901100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, I guess you know which angle I come at Christianity from.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Orthodoxy and Anglicans does have original sin as well. (combined thats over 58% of Christians, but less in the US). So its an awful lot of Christians, even if its not a universal belief.<br /> <br /> By the by, this conversation makes me realize why so many people were shocked and surprised when the Pope recently called himself a sinner. Its not part of their Christianity.<br /> <br /> I have seen a number of conversations on the topic of LS Christianity over the years and this is the most impressive one I have seen to date.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my experience in Christianity is mostly Lutheran, which while it may not have the specific doctrine of Original Sin, is still very much based on the belief that humans are fundamental flawed, sinful, unworthy creatures, and we have to beg God to forgive because we're so wicked. A lot of that stemmed from Martin Luther's own, for lack of a better term, inferiority complex, but it's a prevalent part of Lutheran worship. Every Lutheran Church service I went to had a bit with everyone saying &quot;We confess we are in bondage to sin and cannot free ourselves,&quot; and so on. So, the Lancea et Sanctum idea that humanity must be driven to the arms of God by literal monsters would appeal, in some respects, to Lutheran as well.<br /> <br /> But yes, I'm wonderfully impressed we've managed to have such an educated discussion about real-world religion as it pertains to game systems without anyone getting offended, or being offending. Well done, everyone!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T17:28:35-07:00","id":901551,"title":"","content":"As someone who was raised in Catholicism, I can look at the Lancea et Sanctum and follow their theology from point A to point B to point C. Its twisted and circuitous and I may not agree with their conclusions, but their footing is solid and not really that much crazier than other real Catholic heresies. In order to convert anyone, believer or non, you have to have a compelling pitch. Part of that is going to be some level of theological consistency. <br /> <br /> One thing that I think gets people hung up is the assumption that everyone who joins the Lancea et Sanctum was a devout Christian before they were embraced and that all devout Christians get their LeS member card upon being embraced. This isn't true. The LeS offers an answer to those who are seeking spiritual meaning in their undead state, an answer which is going to appeal to different people for different reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:01:30-07:00","id":901587,"title":"","content":"I see the discussion in this thread as inspiration for how a Jewish or Islamic Covenant would get started. A bunch of vampires of the faith hashing it out over what it now means to be a 'good' vampire in regards to their faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T17:12:59-07:00","id":903120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=901100#post901100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, I guess you know which angle I come at Christianity from.<br /> <br /> That being said, the Orthodoxy and Anglicans does have original sin as well. (combined thats over 58% of Christians, but less in the US). So its an awful lot of Christians, even if its not a universal belief.<br /> <br /> By the by, this conversation makes me realize why so many people were shocked and surprised when the Pope recently called himself a sinner. Its not part of their Christianity.<br /> <br /> I have seen a number of conversations on the topic of LS Christianity over the years and this is the most impressive one I have seen to date.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just not so. It's just the opposite. Most Protestants believe in original sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:14:26-07:00","id":903535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=900463#post900463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Mohammed, like Jesus, was a prophet sent to <i>humanity</i>. Not the Kindred. If the Kindred do not have their own prophet, and the teachings of Mohammed do not apply to them, then they're pretty much stuck in the same situation as the Sanctum. . . basically making it up for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it might not be something most of today's Muslims think about much, if at all, Islam technically accepts the notion of nonhuman adherents; no theology prevents vampires from believing that Muhammad's message could be for them as well.<br /> <br /> A while back, there was a thread about a covenant whose goal was to reconcile the vampiric condition with the sharia, and determine how each should be adapted to allow for the other. In practice, they'd be the ones making sure the vampiric and human worlds flow together smoothly (which includes being upholders of the Masquerade, and probably dealings with other supernaturals) - so more comparable to the Invictus or Carthians than the Lancea. My own contribution was suggesing that the judgments they make about the way vampires should live manifest in similar fashion to Carthian Law - but maybe with more heft, scaled up to a quasi-Discipline. How they might answer some of the questions in the OP:<ul><li>You want to join us because God and His world have not changed, and we can offer you a way for you to remain the person that they made. [Significance: it's not Islamic or religious feeling they use to recruit, it's the desire to retain and feel your Humanity; it's a Muslim covenant only because of the extent to which Islam affects the surrounding human culture (does this make it more an analogue to Masquerade's Camarilla than any Requiem covenant?)]</li> <li>We came from the fear of existing vampiric orders in the time of the Prophet, where they embraced members of the new faith to gain power over it - but God's truth was too strong, so instead it was the faith that taught the vampires how to live.</li> <li>Nicknames might include Faithful or the Judges; derogatory nicknames might include Weaklings, given how little they embrace their vampiric nature.</li> <li>When we are in power, we do not need to exercise power; we determine the bounds of power. Above all, domains where this covernant rules are <i>quiet</i>: the simplest form of the covenant's goals is prevent the vampire and human communities from inflicting undue harm on one another. A common knock-on effect is that vampires are often all-or-nothing in their interactions with humans - either living as human lives as they can, and suppressing their natures as much as possible - or if they have vampiric concerns to pursue, doing so far away from people, crossing paths with them only when they need to feed. [So a covenant like the Lancea, which requires both monstrosity and an interest in humans, would be surpressed under this regime]</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> All that said, a covenant like this shouldn't be the only &quot;Islamic&quot; covenant. One that's more rooted in a purpose from God, whether one similar to the Lancea or a different one, could easily coexist (if uneasily) with it.<br /> <br /> On the other hand:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Allah did not send the Kindred a Prophet, why? What are they supposed to do with His lack of divine guidance? How do they fit into Allah's grand plan, and what can they do to aid it? </div> </div> </div>There are other forces in the world that demand worship. False gods that seek to tempt men away from God's truth. But God has turned His gaze - His light, His sight, His judgment and His truth away from you - you are capable now of neither good nor evil - but the false gods will not know this. You can sate them, keep them lazy and satisfied so they will not seek their worship from those in the light. These deeds are not part of your life, and you will not be judged for them at the end of time - <i>we</i> will judge you now if you abuse this privilege, but that's different. Should you need to kill, for your own sustenance or that of the false gods, take only the most virtuous - those who the true God will look on with favour at the moment of their deaths.<br /> <br /> Sort of like if Belial's Brood was distracting Belial from getting human cultists, and scapegoating themselves for the rest of civilisation. I have no idea if that makes any sense from an Islamic perspective, but it came to me reading what you wrote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I know of Judaism, one of the fundamental tenets is that the Jewish people are God's chosen. Are vampires made from Jews then &quot;un-chosen,&quot; or are they chosen for something else? </div> </div> </div>The Nephilim were mentioned earlier on, as a place where Judaic-inspired Kindred might meet learn their forbidden arts. The Nephilim are also in some texts associated with Azazel, to whom the scapegoat was sent. Could a Jewish covenant see their feeding in a light similar to the scapegoat? A sacrifice into which the sin and uncleanness of the people is poured - hence it being carried out through the consumption of blood - so as to obviate those sins. Vampires are unclean, but that's not really the point of the covenant. They draw uncleanness out of people along with the blood, making it a right and duty to feed on humans (at low blood potency, they eshew animals, at high blood potency they may fall into torpor or continue to feed on humans even though their actual sustenance comes from Kindred). When the story of Longinus started spreading about, those who believed in Jesus's divinity also had to believe that the sacrifical purpose of their feeding had been carried out in another way, and had to find a new way to express their sense of purpose, hence the testing regime of the Lancea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T09:25:11-07:00","id":910870,"title":"","content":"Hello, nice discussion.<br /> <br /> I remember another person that tried to make a Muslim covenant, but he was actually describing &quot;good Muslim kine&quot; rather than &quot;vampires&quot;.<br /> <br /> Making a parallel with the spear we can see it like a sort of a crazy and scary organization. They think to be Demons, and they act like them, they are not humans, they are not sinners anymore, they are already condemned to live the Hell on earth, forever, and they deserved that punishment for the sins they have made as humans.<br /> <br /> I think if we want to build some gritty and dark covenant we have not to debate on theological stuff (like the original sin) but take inspiration from the surface of those culture and religions, without taking everything from them.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Jewish covenant:<br /> <br /> Watchers of the Alliance<br /> <br /> They think to be punished for breaking the rules of the pact, but instead of being totally destroyed they were made as tools of God. They are extremely well connected with the kine and the most connected with the rest of the world. They vigil on their own people (but they may &quot;punish&quot; them hard if they think they are doing something that breaks the Alliance) and help them to get richness and power and, sometimes, force them to give birth, they want to form a strong population that in a future could become a fearful force.<br /> But they do it in the shadow. They are not so strong right now, they are too few. They usually don't try to get directly the power inside of the vampiric community, but they infiltrate in other covenants trying to have subordinate positions, but with the influence that they need to perpetuate their agenda.<br /> They believe that vampirism had born only after the fall of the temple and only to jews, and the diffusion of the vampirism to other people was a mistake of the firsts vampires.<br /> <br /> story: They have formed thousand of years ago, after the fall of the Temple of Jerusalem. They formed group in Khazaria, but they had hard times over there, then they moved in Poland, where they were pretty strong untill wwII.<br /> There were communities in Spain and France, but they had really hard times (in Spain), in Italy they were completely wiped out by Lancea. <br /> The diaspora forced them to move everywhere, today they are especially present in Israel,North America, France, Uk, Russia and where are present, usually, jewish communities. There is, strangely, a growing community of them in China.<br /> <br /> They don't feed on jews, but they are merciless with all other kines.<br /> They developed rituals that can permit them to build clay robots (golem-like).<br /> <br /> <br /> Muslim Covenant:<br /> <br /> I created them as an &quot;antagonist&quot; covenant, like the VII.<br /> <br /> Cult of Isis / Dark Mujaheddin<br /> <br /> They masked themselves as a branch of the Circle, to get more adept. The neophytes don't know much of the real intent of the covenant, but they are attracted by the strict rules of it after they are get lost in a unlife of immorality and seek some sense in it.<br /> Even if they claim to worship Isis there aren't any kind of idols of her, and they are banned. &quot;She is too pure to be seen&quot; they say to the neophytes. But, gradually, they discover the truth behind it, if they are considered worth.<br /> <br /> They are a really recent covenant, most of them are young vampires and when they were humans usually they were not religious. they believe that the vampires were made by Iblis (the devil) to plague humanity so to turn back to the grace of Allah they have to destroy all the vampire, or die while they try to destroy at least one.<br /> <br /> They say that touching a woman (kine or vampire) or even looking her face is an impure thing to do, unless she is considered immoral. And that thing happens a lot of time. In that case the rule is not applied. For this reason most of them are male and the women that join in have to hide completely their faces.<br /> <br /> They developed an unstable blood magic that permit them to make their blood boiling or burn and, when they are unlucky, explode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:23:41-07:00","id":911092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brighella</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=910870#post910870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They vigil on their own people (but they may &quot;punish&quot; them hard if they think they are doing something that breaks the Alliance) and help them to get richness and power and, sometimes, force them to give birth, they want to form a strong population that in a future could become a fearful force.<br /> But they do it in the shadow. They are not so strong right now, they are too few. They usually don't try to get directly the power inside of the vampiric community, but they infiltrate in other covenants trying to have subordinate positions, but with the influence that they need to perpetuate their agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Just no.<br /> <br /> We do not need &quot;Zionist Conspiracy Theory Bankers&quot; the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T02:05:51-07:00","id":1140456,"title":"","content":"NOTE: I wrote this for another similar thread, I figured it would make sense to post it here, too. If you see some references to what others have said, it might be from the other thread.<br /> <br /> Hi, everybody,<br /> <br /> I am Muslim and I bumped into this thread as I was planning to narrate a chronicle set in Cordoba in the year 1000 CE, so culturally-Muslim vampires will feature heavily.<br /> <br /> Note: I only became aware of the Banu Shaytan and Iblic Creed stuff reading your posts, and I am going to check them out immediately. Thank you.<br /> <br /> First, to be clear: Islam's abrogations of previous revelations does not mean they stop being true and of divine origin. It simply means that the norms they set are no more binding and that, if they say something explicitly denied by the Quran (such as Jesus - peace be upon him - being the Son of God), that is to be considered a human addition. Beyond this, Muslims throughout history, even pious ones reputed to be saints/walis, have had all sorts of attitudes to previous religions. Also, there are some Muslims who do not believe in abrogation and see previous religions as still valid, though they are few and criticized for this. They exist, nonetheless, so Muslim-cultured Kindred might well claim similar ideas.<br /> <br /> My personal take on the Lancea et Sanctum as seen by vampires in Muslim lands is this: when Islam appeared, the Byzantine Empire was mostly Sanctified (i.e.: LeS), Arabia was Circle of the Crone and Persia (Zoroastrianism) was CotC or something else (still need to figure it out, since Persian stuff does not feature in my Cordoba chronicle).<br /> Early human converts to Islam, once embraced, would not find Muslim guides in their vampirism. The closest thing they would find were Sanctified teachers. Longinism would make more sense to them than adapting Islam to vampirism because:<br /> 1) Islam's religious precepts are evidently not appliable to vampires;<br /> 2) only God can issue religious norms, so vampires can't just take the five pillars, dietary restrictions and other rules and adapt them to vampires (like five prayers at night, don't drink blood of drunkards or pig-eaters, starve to torpor/frenzy in Ramadan, etc), as one would need divine authority for that. Regarding the prayers, I prefer not making them perform any of the five daily prayers, not even the night ones, on the basis that, drinking human blood and being more or less walking corpses, they would be considered ritually impure in various schools of Islamic law, thus being forbidden from performing the five obligatory prayers (although they can perform other forms of prayer that do not require ritual purity, such as dhikr - the remembrance of God - or dua - supplication and personal conversation with God);<br /> 3) Muslims acknowledge previous prophets, including Jesus (peace be upon him), so the tale of Longinus receiving guidance can work. Theologically, he may be classed as a wali (saint) from the community of Jesus, as opposed to a prophet in the strict Islamic theological sense, and this would make things easier;<br /> 4) surah al-Jinn (72nd surah of the Quran) says some Jinn were listening to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) once while he was reciting the Quran and recognised its divine origin. In general, Jinn are believed to be of different kinds, to descend from Iblis/Lucifer/the Devil/Shaytan/Satan, to be responsible for part of polytheism (as jinns made humans worship them as gods), to be able to mate with humans and have offspring from them at times, to have free will, to follow different religions - the same humans follow, since, as far as I learnt, they do not get their own prophets but are guided by human prophets and saints, hence the idea of Longinus being a wali/saint instead of a vampire prophet. Muslim-cultured vampires may see themselves as a sub-species of Jinn (the Strix may well be another sub-species), especially if this is how Arabian pre-Islamic vampires saw themselves. Whichever vampire claimed to have interacted with the Prophet (peace be upon him) or his Companions and received instructions from them may have simply said that the main order was to carry on with Longinism, just knowing that Jesus is not God or His Son, etc., but without prescribed rules that differ from Longinism;<br /> 5) the Quran and the Hadith do not mention (to my knowledge) what rules Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) set for the Jinn, although it's generally understood that they did receive rules from him and previous prophets (peace be upon them all), so whatever rules Longinism imposes on vampires, that can be claimed as the rules set for them;<br /> 6) Longinism does not see Longinus as God, but only as a kind of prophet. This does not overtly contrast the Islamic creed, although it would make it slightly in theological debates easier to see Longinus as a wali/saint or sort of mystical disciple of Jesus. As a wali, he could still receive visions and inspirations, though there are some slight theological differences between walis and prophets.<br /> 7) there are various interpretations of the verses of the Quran about the crucifixion. It's enough to say that Longinian &quot;Muslim&quot; vampires stick to the view that Jesus (peace be upon him) was put on the cross, pierced by Longinus, and then taken up to heaven (before dying). <br /> <br /> In my setting, a Lancea et Sanctum Council was called in Damascus in 800 CE and established that the Church of Longinus was independent of the developments of human religions and its members were free to believe that Muhammad (peace be upon him) was a prophet or not, settling the issue for most adherents (obviously there can always be minor conflicts and divisions here and there, but they don't entail the forming of a wholly different Covenant). Moreover, vampires were not meant to push humans to one or the other Abrahamic religion, as this could effectively harm the appeal of that religion, but only remind humans of God, making them fear Him, tempt them to test them, and fight the Circle of the Crone and any vampire who promoted polytheism or atheism.<br /> <br /> I assume that there are vampires who carry on their mortal religion (whether Islam or Christianity or Judaism or other), but these usually act alone and have not formed proper Covenants that can rival with the LeS. It is quite common for new vampires, too, to hang onto one's mortal religion for a while, but this is usually temporary. One exception that I plan to include in the Chronicle is a group of vampire vampire-hunters called &quot;at-Tawwabun&quot; (the Repentant), who believe the only way to be forgiven by God is by killing other vampires and feeding only from animals forbidden to Muslims (ex.: pigs and predatory animals). This would be an antagonist covenant, however, not open to players. I have more interesting ideas about them, but I'll share them in time, God willing.<br /> <br /> In my Cordoba, the Bishop/Great Imam of the Lancea et Sanctum/ar-Rumh wal-Quds (I use double names to reflect the double culture of the vampires of Muslim Spain) has imposed on the city's vampire to feed only from sinful humans and not to kill the kine, unless they were condemned to death by the human authorities. In addition to this, Longinians are encouraged to shepherd the flock they belonged to in life (vampires who were Muslim prey on Muslims and vampires who were Christian prey on Christians), as they are most likely to understand how to remind their victims of God, but this is only an encouragement.<br /> <br /> I hope all the above makes sense. I am going to read the material about the Banu Shaytan and see how that is, God willing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:35:59-07:00","id":1140646,"title":"","content":"Being an ex-Muslim I might give some help detailing Ibn-Shaitan, first by saying that it should be changed to Abna Al-Shaitan, or perhaps Banu Shaitan, even better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:28:40-07:00","id":1140942,"title":"","content":"Since they are all pretty similar anyway (from the perspective of a non religious person), you could always say that the Lancea is not so monolithic as they appear in the books and that local chapters are free to use elements of any Abrahamic religion in their rites.<br /> <br /> This way you don't have to design a whole new covenant, just the rites they perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 09-16-2017, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T13:45:25-07:00","id":1141523,"title":"","content":"Not sure the Jewish one should even focus on Jewish theology, per se.<br /> <br /> How about a Sect that is focused more on protecting and propagating the Jewish people, community and traditions in a vampiric context? Maybe a Carthian-related group that emulates mid-century Israeli kibbutzim?<br /> <br /> They could see themselves as both defenders of the Jewish community in the direct sense of fighting anti-Semites, but also providing a better environment for Jewish vampires.<br /> <br /> So, they would enter smaller cities where life is hard for a vampire and build communal systems of blood gathering, storage, and distribution that is done in as ethical a manner as possible. I can picture long, complex debates of what constitutes an ethical system for blood gathering, but that would become an interesting part of the story. Whatever the methods, it would be their version of making the desert bloom... and the underlying assumption for all these debates would be that one should live by the law, not die by it.<br /> <br /> They could help vampires establish havens that are ethically acquired and pleasant to reside in, not stolen squats or rancid sewers. This could be where much of the communal life of the community occurs.<br /> <br /> The other service they would provide is simple networking. Just because you're a vampire doesn't mean your mortal beliefs and practices vanish. For lot of Jewish practices a minyan is needed. It could be nearly impossible, except in a very few cities, to put together a minyan of Jewish vampires. For most Jews, even if you're a vampire, it's nice to know that if you have an unfortunate sunlight-related accident, somebody, somewhere will be saying Kaddish and sitting Shiva.<br /> <br /> On a pastoral level a community that is focused on personal ethics and maintaining ties to the mortal community could also be helpful with the retention of humanity. Even vampires from the goyim might find benefits from a fairly level-headed, practical community of vampires.<br /> <br /> Of course, it's hard to imagine all of this happening in the context of the more Orthodox interpretations of law, but the Reformed and Reconstructionist? Maybe.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm saying make it less a religious cult and more a late-night JCC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T10:11:15-07:00","id":1141801,"title":"","content":"Focus less on the requirement to be ethical in acquiring blood and I could see this so much<br /> <br /> EDIT: I say this because I have the feeling that every Covenant should at least have at least some strong potential for villainy baked right into the ideology.<br /> The Lancea Sanctum think themselves monsters, the Circle of the Crone worships the monsters they are, the Invictus are literally blood-sucking feudal overlords, the Ordo have no requirement to care about ethics and the Carthians can follow monstrous ideologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 09-19-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T13:29:10-07:00","id":1141873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1141523#post1141523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm saying make it less a religious cult and more a late-night JCC.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf you go with a jewish community, then wouldn't you be making a kind of miniture city? Rather than just one covenant, you'd be dealing with a couple covenants all with a jewish slant to them - either as local varations of the main five, or unique ones?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1141801#post1141801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Focus less on the requirement to be ethical in acquiring blood and I could see this so much<br /> <br /> EDIT: I say this because I have the feeling that every Covenant should at least have at least some strong potential for villainy baked right into the ideology.<br /> The Lancea Sanctum think themselves monsters, the Circle of the Crone worships the monsters they are, the Invictus are literally blood-sucking feudal overlords, the Ordo have no requirement to care about ethics and the Carthians can follow monstrous ideologies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Just a side note - the innate monstrocity of the Carthians isn't that they're potentially following monstrous idealologies, its that they're idealologies that don't account for innate mind control abilities. Want democracy for the dead? Sure. The Majesty specialists pretty much drool over that idea - swaying crowds like that is like breathing to them. Its that you have a group of inantely violative people who are tugged by their emotions and desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T15:53:16-07:00","id":1141923,"title":"","content":"I read an article: <a href=\"https://www.themarysue.com/mother-is-a-fascinating-film-better-understood-if-you-consider-the-jews/\" target=\"_blank\">full of spoilers for the film mother!</a>. While the film doesn't suggest anything for a vampiric covenant (though it really captures how I feel about parties), the article I linked to goes into some characteristics of the Jewish relationship with God that might be useful to think about when crafting a Jewish vampiric covenant.<br /> <br /> In particular, a Jewish-based covenant might be more willing to consider their damnation - or however else they characterise their condition - as unjust on God's part. Which could change a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T20:05:17-07:00","id":1142014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1141873#post1141873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf you go with a jewish community, then wouldn't you be making a kind of miniture city? Rather than just one covenant, you'd be dealing with a couple covenants all with a jewish slant to them - either as local varations of the main five, or unique ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's something of an inherent problem where there isn't a Jewish population to support this. Israel is the only place with a concentrated enough Jewish population (both religious identifying and cultural/ethnic/etc. identifying) where Jewish community culture really has a chance to flourish and would mostly express itself as local variations on the Invictus, Carthians, and Ordo; assuming there isn't an Israeli Jewish answer to the LeS and CotC.<br /> <br /> Even in the US, where there's enough Jews to have a significant number of Jewish vampires, they'd be too spread out to really form meaningful communities. New York, Los Angeles, and Miami are the only US cities where you could realistically end up with 10+ Jewish vampires unless there's a massive disproportionate Embracing of Jews by someone.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons to look towards a Jewish equivalent to the LeS is that it can be less sensitive to Jewish population shifts. A community focused Jewish vampire organization has no reason to stick around in Europe with so few Jews left after the Holocaust. A mystic oriented one might have caches or sacred sites that were hundreds of years old that they'd be interested in upkeeping ever after there aren't lots of Jews around to concentrate on directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1141923#post1141923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read an article: <a href=\"https://www.themarysue.com/mother-is-a-fascinating-film-better-understood-if-you-consider-the-jews/\" target=\"_blank\">full of spoilers for the film mother!</a>. While the film doesn't suggest anything for a vampiric covenant (though it really captures how I feel about parties), the article I linked to goes into some characteristics of the Jewish relationship with God that might be useful to think about when crafting a Jewish vampiric covenant.<br /> <br /> In particular, a Jewish-based covenant might be more willing to consider their damnation - or however else they characterise their condition - as unjust on God's part. Which could change a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that link. I haven't gone to seen mother! because I wasn't drawn to worrying about seeing it in theaters, but that's an extremely interesting response to it. And I agree that the read itself could be a very interesting inspiration for how Jewish vampires might frame their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:19:51-07:00","id":1142092,"title":"","content":"The LeS have the Testament of Longinus, right? I could easily see a Muslim equivalent having some piece of scripture that (they claim) was revealed to Muhammad but that he was told to leave out of the mainstream Qur'an as it was instructions specifically for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:43:19-07:00","id":1142099,"title":"","content":"Or add another vampire prophet with the justification that Muhammad was the final <i>human</i> prophet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:54:37-07:00","id":1142101,"title":"","content":"Two factions. One claim it was the former, the other claim it was the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T05:18:28-07:00","id":1142105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1142014#post1142014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's something of an inherent problem where there isn't a Jewish population to support this.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes and no? Supernatural demographics aren't necessarily matching up to mortal ones. Heck, if a jewish vampire is the most powerful one in the area, they could very well have enough influence to build a community when one doesn't exist among humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T05:36:44-07:00","id":1142108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1142099#post1142099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or add another vampire prophet with the justification that Muhammad was the final <i>human</i> prophet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, not inconceivable given that we're dealing with evil, blood sucking monsters... but, for anyone who had even a nominal relationship to Islam in their breathing days, the idea that revelation is sealed is a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> The idea is that everything that needed to be revealed was revealed, and within that revelation it said unambiguously that revelation wassealed. Anyone who comes along afterward saying otherwise might seem like they were calling the Quran (and therefore the divine source of the Quran) either capable of making major mistakes in what is revealed, or of lying in those revelations. This implication would be a non-starter for nearly anyone, anywhere in the umma, alive or undead.<br /> <br /> Now, that said, having a small group of individual vampires come together and form a new Madhhab, or school of interpretation of Islam, and, therefore, a new interpretation of fiqh, or human understanding of divine law, could be possible. There are Surahs that say the Prophet was sent to teach both humanity and the Jinn, so if the vampiric school of Islamic jurisprudence conceptualized the Beast as a personal Jinn... well, I don't know enough about Muslim folklore or scripture to take all that to its logical conclusion, but I think it could work.<br /> <br /> The main problem I can see is that, like any field of jurisprudence, new rulings are ordinarily based on precedent, and different mortal Madhhab have different existing precedent, though there are large areas of overlap. This means that they would first need to decide which school the Vampiric Madhhab grew from, so there was a body of precedent to work with. This choice would immediately tend to exclude, or at least discourage, vampires with sympathies to other schools. It's hard to imagine getting Sufi, Salafi and Ahmadiyya vampires to exist side by side in a single religion-based vampiric organization, even if they are all blood-drinkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:38:01-07:00","id":1142167,"title":"","content":"And the idea that Jesus didn't die for your sins is likewise a theoretical non-starter for many Christians who go undead. And yet, its a thing. Vampire religions don't have to hold onto even the central doctrine of human religions. That's not what they do. <br /> <br /> Having a vampire who lived at the same time as Muhammad could work. Or having Muhammad become a vampire after finishing his farewell pilgrimage. Or even when alive just having &quot;secret teachings&quot; that never made it to mortal ears. We could even just go neutral and call the final prophet, well, The Prophet and leave the exact nature of who this was a mystery and let vampires argue it out ICly. Lead to divisions and internal strife. That kind of thing is good for the stories, after all. <br /> <br /> From a game design standpoint, who delivered the teachings is frankly unimportant. Vampire games are concerned with the night-to-night affairs, and so what's important is the night-to-night operation of the vampires who follow this faith, not the details of historical theology. Given the nature of Vampire as a city-based game, and how each and every city should have a different take on the core system? Going into these details are actually detrimental instead of beneficial. <br /> <br /> Should there be a central prophet figure from the time of Muhammad, possibly the man himself? Yes. Even if its a different person, should the actions of this vampire-Prophet mirror Muhammad? Yes, but as a distorted mirror. And what did He teach to the jinn, who had set themselves up as gods? What actions differ? What precepts should there be? These are the important details that seem to be glossed over in favor of arguing about Muhammad or not. <br /> <br /> From a purely game design standpoint, we cannot have vampires following the exact same tenants as actual Islam. That's not how Vampire works, and it would be a disaster anyways. There has to be deviation. What's important is finding what those deviations are, and how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:48:26-07:00","id":1142307,"title":"","content":"My personal approach has been to: 1) set aside the law-aspect per se considering that most Islamic norms don't work on vampires and they would even seem impure (blood in corpse) fiqh wise and I found it boring and plain weird to just invent a vampire version of Shari'ah; 2) focus on the concept of being tasked to remind mortals of God; 3) avoid to implicate the Prophet - peace be upon him - explicitly in all this, but that is my personal thing as a Muslim to avoid disrespecting (even in fiction) or lying about (even if fiction) what the Prophet (peace be upon him) did.<br /> <br /> Point 3 is obviously totally personal, so you may disregard it, and, on a note, in my take on the Longinus story I try to keep Jesus (peace be upon him) equally out of it, again, out of respect (even in running a game) for God's prophets (peace be upon them all). Of course, the story for the LeS is that it was through the blood of Christ that Longinus was cursed, but that can be dealt with. First, Jesus need not have been intending that to happen. It could be God's curse. Second, it may simply be the LeS belief, while in reality Longinus may have been embraced by someone else and mixed up things or lied.<br /> <br /> That being said, one could totally make a Muslim covenant whose founders CLAIMED to have received special instructions from the Prophet sall Allahu alayhi wasallam.<br /> <br /> I personally didn't want to simply repropose among vampires the same divisions humans have. I thought it nicer to think of the LeS as something so unique to vampires that it let its adherents put totally in second place the issue of which Abrahamic religion the vampire used to follow. It makes sense though that even Christians (non-Longinians), Jew and Muslim vampires have each their own covenants, but I just prefer avoiding that in my Chronicle, unless they're small, unorganized groups of vampires who don't reach the size and structure of an international Covenant.<br /> <br /> I was reading the Testament of Longinus recently though and there are explicit mentions of the divinity of Jesus, even as something that a Longinian MUST believe (see the Rule of Golgotha). Now, that's clearly a problem for Jews and Muslims. However, they could &quot;neglect&quot; that specific part of the Testament. Both Jew and Muslim Longinians for example could argue that Longinus used the term Son of God in the sense of an extremely dear and honored servant of God, or Muslim Longinians may say that even the Testament of Longinus, while being a revelation, was subject to alteration and that one should disregard in it those things that are denied by the Quran, while accepting the rest, thus putting aside the issue of divinity of Jesus. This would clearly create some tension in the LeS, but overall they would remain within the fold of the LeS, with the tensions being more or less intense depending on the city one is in. This is pretty much how the Iblic and Dammitic creed are dealt with in the LeS covenant book.<br /> <br /> Another alternative comes to my mind too, but that suits probably Muslim players more than others. There's a story (in the real world, not in WoD) about a Companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him) who happened to actually ingest the Prophet's blood. He had been ordered to bury it, like Muslims do with bodily parts that are detached from the body like nails, etc., but instead he decided to ingest it hoping it would be blessed (the Prophet's body is reported to have had miraculous properties, such as his sweat having a beautiful smell, his touch leaving things perfumed, his saliva having healing properties, ecc) and he was told that, due to having ingested the blood, even if he should not have done it (since he had been told to bury it), the Fire (i.e.: Hell) would not touch him. Now, this runs opposite to the Longinus narrative in the LeS: taste Jesus' blood and get cursed, even if there is a significant distinction: Longinus tasted the blood out of gluttony, laziness and perversion, while that Companion ingested it out of over-whelming love and faith (like the lady who touches Jesus' robe and is healed in the Gospels, just slightly weirder...).<br /> <br /> The two stories of Longinus and this Companion could have been merged by a uniquely Muslim vampire covenant (not necessarily the only Muslim covenant) who claims that Longinus' curse was a mercy from God to the Kindred, that they may be guided in their vampiric state, while they could have that blood of the Prophet (peace be upon him), transmitted through his descendants (so it could be a Shi'i inclined covenant, but not necessarily: many sunnis equally revere the Prophet's descendants, they just don't agree that they had to be the political leaders of the community by necessity), has the power to cure vampirism or lessen the curse somehow, provided one takes it out of reverence and faith and not meaning to harm the Prophet's descendants (who may themselves be immune to vampirism, dying automatically if they're embraced and not becoming ghoul even if force-fed vitae). So Longinus is there to guide the Kindred, while the Ahl al-Bayt (the Prophet's descendants) are there to lessen their curse or remove it if they're repentant and faithful. This Covenant would vow itself to protect the Ahlu l-Bayt through their vampiric might, until they are considered ready to receive pardon and taste enough prophetic blood to return human. While on the journey to redemption through service of the Ahlu l-Bayt, they could have benefits similar to the Coils of the Dragon (lessen the effects of the vampiric curse), but obtained through imbibing small portions of the descendants' blood, willingly offered to their protectors.<br /> <br /> This Covenant would obviously be seen as heretical by the LeS, even if it accepts Longinus' message for vampires who do not feel the call to redemption through service to the Ahlu l-Bayt. <br /> <br /> So, to recap, this Covenant sees two ways for vampires: either a vampire sticks to Longinus' way (be a wolf among the sheep to remind them of God) or he vows himself to service and protection of the Ahlu l-Bayt until he is pardoned and returned human (already in a state of grace for Paradise once natural death comes, probably). The Ahlu l-Bayt's blood, given as a gift and not taken forcefully, and in small quantities bestows different powers that somehow lift or reduce aspects of the curse (like the Coils of the Dragon does, even if it works differenty) until it is completely lifted. These powers could be called Barakaat (blessings) and they are imparted by the Ahlu l-Bayt themselves by some prayer done at the moment of giving the blood, and they also know through kashf (unveiling, a type of inspiration or visions that saints/walis have) when the vampire is ready to receive the ultimate blessing of returning human. In this sense, these Barakaat are more similar to the gifts of the Uratha (bestowed by spirits or by the Moon) than to vampiric disciplines (cultivated by the vampire).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:54:06-07:00","id":1142309,"title":"","content":"A Vampiric Covenant with supernatural human rulers? I am intrigued","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:55:31-07:00","id":1142311,"title":"","content":"Btw, if anyone is wondering why would someone need to bury the Prophet's (peace be upon him) blood... The Prophet used to practice and receive hijamah (wet cupping, where tiny cuts are done on specific parts of the body and then air-compressed cups are applied on those body parts to let the superficial stagnant blood seep out), so the blood was that left in the cup after the cupping, if I remember the story correctly. Wet cupping is still practiced worldwide, just like dry cupping (which comes from chinese acupuncture and is more popular). The difference is just whether one lets the blood out or not. Note that it's not the same as European bloodletting, as the amount of blood, the places where the blood is taken from, the methods employed to extract it, the medical theory behind it and even the frequency with which it is performed (hijamah is performed on specific days and not too frequently) are totally different. The only thing in common between the two is the idea of removing &quot;old&quot; or &quot;stagnant&quot; blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T15:05:31-07:00","id":1142315,"title":"","content":"That is a very intriguing idea for a Covenant, Hermeticus! Very cool, and definitely an interesting juxtaposition. Out of curiousity, how do you imagine these Kindred perceive the necessity of feeding on other humans? Is it discouraged? An acknowledged necessity? Ritualized in some other fashion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T22:00:30-07:00","id":1142414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1142315#post1142315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a very intriguing idea for a Covenant, Hermeticus! Very cool, and definitely an interesting juxtaposition. Out of curiousity, how do you imagine these Kindred perceive the necessity of feeding on other humans? Is it discouraged? An acknowledged necessity? Ritualized in some other fashion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, Leetsepeak!<br /> <br /> Since, as I presented them, they accept Longinianism in principle (probably with the only exception of the divinity of Jesus - peace beupon him) and they simply take an alternative path to redemption (instead of just seeing themselves as Damned), they would in general apply the &quot;wolf among the sheep&quot; Longinian idea, i.e.: they are allowed and indeed required to feed off human (as long as they're not Ahlu l-Bayt of course, as they're blood must be received as a gift and blessing, not taken) as part of their mandate to remind humans of God. They would see it as: &quot;God has made the blood of humans (and of vampires, if one's blood potency is too high to feed from humans) halal (lawful) to us as He has made the flesh of animals halal to human beings, and just as He commanded humans to eat and drink but without exceeding, He has commanded us to drink, without exceeding. Just as He has commanded humans to invoke His Name before slaughtering the animals and before eating, as a reminder that it is only by His permission that they can kill them for their survival, so must we invoke His Name before we drink of the blood of the Children of Adam.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would probably include the idea that they must not kill their victims, but only drink what they need. This is an idea that I would apply to the LeS in general though, as I don't see killing one's victims much in line with &quot;reminding them of God&quot;. They may perhaps be allowed to kill when feeding from someone who has already been condemned to the death penalty by mortal authorities for some religious transgression. I include as a condition the fact of having been condemned by mortal authorities because usually, if one commits a transgression for which there is the possibility of capital punishment in Islamic Law, but they're not caught and repent, they're actually not meant to be punished, as they're not being caught is seen as God covering their sin and accepting their repentance. Confessing the sin publicly in these cases is considered as more damaging to society and to the individual than just keeping it between oneself and God. Therefore I wouldn't see Muslim vampires as preying on and killing people who have committed egregious transgressors but have not been caught by the authorities (they're not Daredevil, basically). Of course a known and unrepentant sinner is the perfect target for a scare feeding, so that he may remember God and repent, but that's without killing him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T22:03:22-07:00","id":1142415,"title":"","content":"For example, the fact that vampiric saliva can heal the wound caused by the bite is in itself a good evidence of the fact that vampires are not meant to kill, but only to take what is needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T22:08:20-07:00","id":1142416,"title":"","content":"In terms of the Embrace, they would probably see it as a tool to punish somebody who really does not want to repent, despite many reminders, hoping that the curse makes them understand how precious being human is and the consequences and gravity of sin, so that maybe they repent as vampires. In that sense, it's almost a mercy, extending the (un)lifespan of a human being on the brink of Hell to give him some extra chance at repentance. So these vampires see themselves as both damned (with vampirism) and graced (with a second chance) at the same time.<br /> <br /> One thing that contributes to their feeling damned is the fact that they cannot perform the regular prayers. Not only they are asleep through the day, but even at night they see themselves as physically impure, because blood (once outside of the veins of its rightful owner) and corpses are ritually impure in Shari'ah, meaning that one cannot perform the canonical five prayers (salah) or other prayers in the same format (I mean with recitation of the Quran, bowings and prostrations) if one has blood over himself (one should wash it away before praying, unless it's impossible for some good reason, in which case one is excused and can pray with it) or is touching a corpse (for example, it is disliked to pray in a cemetery because one is practically standing on corpses), so vampires would be a walking impurity. They can still invoke God through supplication and remember Him (through the practice of dhikr, the repetition of divine names or formulas, similar to mantras in some respects), but they are cut off from the main form of prayer (the salah), not to mention the Pilgrimage. In fact, one of the Barakaat that the Ahlu l-Bayt could bestow on them (in something like a Coil of Worship, keeping the Coils of the Dragon system) is the capacity to be ritually purified by their blood in order to perform the salah or even the Pilgrimage (a high level power could even make the vampire free from the need to feed and immune to sunlight for just as long as it will take him or her to perform the Pilgrimage from outside the sanctuary area of Mecca (that would be a couple of weeks). This, for example, could be something done when one is close to be returned human, as a way to cleanse oneself totally of sins (through the Pilgrimage) and foretaste the return to mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 09-21-2017, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T02:57:38-07:00","id":1142442,"title":"","content":"The only concern I have here is that I like my Chronicles of Darkness to be a bit... theologically murky. &quot;Follow this Islam-based covenant and you can become human again&quot; seems a little too clear-cut on the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T05:29:48-07:00","id":1142470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1142442#post1142442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only concern I have here is that I like my Chronicles of Darkness to be a bit... theologically murky. &quot;Follow this Islam-based covenant and you can become human again&quot; seems a little too clear-cut on the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can always make it something not sure. Maybe it is something the Ahlu l-Bayt say is possible and the Barakaat covenant discipline is a path to that but no vampire is yet known to have attained it, except in second-hand account, like with Golconda. This would be similar to the Ordo Dracul idea of transcendence: they're trying and they have intermediate results (the Coils), but nobody has actually achieved it yet except in tales (except maybe for Dracula).<br /> <br /> I think this covenant would work well in redemption/transcendence Chronicles where characters are looking for Golconda and the like. Maybe instead of returning vampires human, the covenant's powers eventually lead its member to some elevated transcendental state appropriate to redeemed vampires. One could take the Sufi concepts of fana and baqa (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baqaa\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baqaa</a>) and turn them in vampiric lower sense, where fana - lit. extinction - means the extinction of the limits of the curse along with the vampires beast and negative ego, while baqa - lit. permanence - means the permanence of the vampiric boons (mainly the disciplines), now no more limited by blood potency and seen as God's gifts and powers manifested through the redeemed servant. The vampire would strive to reach a specific complete state of no limits (including the threat to one's morality posed by the Beast) but keep the goodies, while in reality one simply gets closer and closer to this state through the various Barakaat that remove or lessen aspects of the Curse, but never actually reach the full deal.<br /> <br /> This makes sense even experience wise: if Barakaat works in a way similar to Coils of the Dragon in 1E, just mastering the three basic coils in the core manual means taking the discipline to level 9.That's 315 XP, and the vampire is not yet free of the curse... So no prob if one wants to keep the players and the characters waiting for the great transcendence moment that never seems to come, but looks always closer...<br /> <br /> If one uses the Ahlu l-Bayt as a sort of special humans who intermediate between all sorts of supernatural creatures in the middle-eastern WoD but are not supernatural themselves (they're not wolf-blooded, they're unghoulable, unembraceable and do not become Awakened nor ghosts - although they still have access to some powers related to faith and miracles and can appear in spirit form to people for guidance even after they're dead), that can grant good plot hooks for plenty of stories involving the whole WoD. Werewolves from the Pure tribes attacking a sayyid (sayyid, or sharif, is the title for individual members of the Ahlu l-Bayt in the Muslim world; the feminine is sayyidah or sharifah, the male plural is saadah or shurafaa, the female plural is sayyidaat or shariifaat); a ghost having decided to haunt a sharifah's room; a young sharif is neglecting his religion and doubting his responsibility as a member of the Ahlu l-Bayt, so an older one asks the coterie to speak to him and show him that the supernatural is real and that he must take on his responsibility; members of ISIS or al-Qa'idah or Boko Haram (who kill Shi'ah and Sufis and therefore possibly people from the Ahlu l-Bayt way before they even look at the West) have kidnapped or are besieging an area with many shurafa, so the characters must go and save them from the terrorists.... The possibilities are endless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T05:35:40-07:00","id":1142474,"title":"","content":"But, as I said from the very beginning, this Covenant (at least the way I presented it) is probably more appealing to Muslim players, because it's evidently based on a validation of their belief (assuming they're not anti-Ahlu l-Bayt). One is free to change it. Sufis (and many shurafa are sufis) and Shi'i mystics still are believed to do plenty supernatural things and miracles, so one could give alternate explanations in one's game on how they do them and why they would be able to offer what they do to vampires.<br /> <br /> I don't believe in the whole Da Vinci code theory of Jesus' - peace be upon him - descendants, but if one does, one could have them cure vampires too. Or have some Hindu sadhus do it, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T17:05:24-07:00","id":1142755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1142414#post1142414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would see it as: &quot;God has made the blood of humans (and of vampires, if one's blood potency is too high to feed from humans) halal (lawful) to us as He has made the flesh of animals halal to human beings, and just as He commanded humans to eat and drink but without exceeding, He has commanded us to drink, without exceeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting wrinkle on that could be that the covenant considers it haram to feed on animals, even when your blood potency is low enough to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would probably include the idea that they must not kill their victims, but only drink what they need. This is an idea that I would apply to the LeS in general though, as I don't see killing one's victims much in line with &quot;reminding them of God&quot; </div> </div> </div>Earlier on, I suggested that some covenants might have the idea of only feeding on the virtuous, so that if they are killed, they will be brought to God's side, and vampires' predations will deprive no one of salvation.<br /> <br /> While I'm in the different covenants camp, I do like the idea of yours. If I were to use it, I would probably make it older than either Islam and Christianity, originating in ancient Israel, and find a different figure to use for the progenitor of the mortal bloodlines. (Though they might have &quot;added&quot; prophets over the years - such as Jesus or Muhammad - with the claim that they met with the vampires and reaffirmed their purpose. In such a case, I would remove Longinus, since the only point of using that name is to invoke the idea of the divinity of Jesus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:11:04-07:00","id":1144180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1142755#post1142755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting wrinkle on that could be that the covenant considers it haram to feed on animals, even when your blood potency is low enough to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the blood of otherwise Halal animals? What if they use that coil that lets you raise a ghouled animal into a nutritious, vitae-filled solid meal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T13:37:27-07:00","id":1144188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1144180#post1144180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the blood of otherwise Halal animals? What if they use that coil that lets you raise a ghouled animal into a nutritious, vitae-filled solid meal?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Those animals are for humans, not for us.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T05:01:46-07:00","id":1144346,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=SunlessNick;n1142755]An interesting wrinkle on that could be that the covenant considers it haram to feed on animals, even when your blood potency is low enough to do so.<br /> <br /> Ermmm... I personally don't see that necessary, but of course, that's a possible twist to it. I'd prefer allowing animal feeding because it can be seen as part of Allah's mercy to new vampires (who need time to adjust morally and to develop predatory skills without endangering the masquerade)... Some specific animals could be haram, though, such as animals that are halal to humans (in which case vampires can feed from predatory animals, but not herbivores, as they tend to be halal), or animals that belong to humans (cattle and pets, so a cat or camel without a owner is free game, but not a cow or pig belonging to somebody). Not sure what to do with pigs specifically... Their being impure for consumption is specific to humans in Islamic law, it's not some general thing that would make them impure for non-humans, so vampires (being jinn) don't have a particular reason to avoid them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T03:40:50-07:00","id":1144689,"title":"","content":"Not being able to eat pets or livestock would make it hard to be a city vampire. Though I guess you could eat rats. Don't think pigeons are herbivores, though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T04:50:26-07:00","id":1146023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/872276-making-muslim-based-and-jewish-based-vampire-covenants?p=1144689#post1144689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not being able to eat pets or livestock would make it hard to be a city vampire. Though I guess you could eat rats. Don't think pigeons are herbivores, though</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much... Depending on the city, there could probably be plenty of cats and dogs without a owner. I don't envisage the average city vampire feeding off owned pets anyway, as their absence is easily noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}